WEBVTT

00:00:03.796 --> 00:00:06.148
Young adult Ailey readers.

00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:08.590
The Hound of the Bascavilles.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.022
Sir Arthur Conan Doyle.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:23.674
Copyright Ailey 2010.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:44.438
Chapter 1 James Mortimer comes to Baker Street Mr Sherlock Holmes was at the breakfast table.

00:00:44.498 --> 00:00:46.610
I was by the fire.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.771
I had a walking stick in my hand.

00:00:49.831 --> 00:00:52.592
It was a stranger's stick.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:58.015
Yesterday a stranger came to the house when Holmes and I were out.

00:00:58.075 --> 00:01:00.838
The stranger left his stick.

00:01:00.898 --> 00:01:11.876
There was some writing on it to James Mortimer, M-R-C-S, from his friends of the C-C-H, 1884.

00:01:11.936 --> 00:01:15.078
Who's the stick, Watson?

00:01:15.138 --> 00:01:17.480
But you can't see me.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.898
How do you know what I'm doing?

00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:24.248
I can see your reflection in the window," said Holmes.

00:01:24.308 --> 00:01:28.773
But tell me, Watson, what do you think of our visitor?

00:01:28.832 --> 00:01:33.607
We didn't meet him, so his stick is an important clue for us.

00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:35.494
What do you think?

00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:40.962
I think," I said, that Mortimer is a successful doctor.

00:01:41.022 --> 00:01:44.104
I know that from the letters MRCS.

00:01:44.164 --> 00:01:47.026
Only a doctor can use those letters.

00:01:47.086 --> 00:01:52.310
He's quite old and he's probably a country doctor.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:58.024
He walks a lot because I can see that Dr. Mortimer uses this stick a lot.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.978
Excellent, said Holmes.

00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:06.342
Then we have friends of the CCH.

00:02:06.402 --> 00:02:08.553
A club, I think.

00:02:08.613 --> 00:02:12.525
Perhaps he helped them, and they gave him the stick.

00:02:12.585 --> 00:02:15.126
Congratulations, Watson.

00:02:15.186 --> 00:02:22.310
However, Holmes continued, I'm sorry, but most of your ideas are wrong.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:23.880
Wrong?

00:02:23.939 --> 00:02:28.872
Well, he's a country doctor and he walks a lot, you're right.

00:02:28.932 --> 00:02:34.565
But I think the CC-8 is probably Charing Cross Hospital, not a club.

00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:37.196
I also think he's a young doctor.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:41.098
He left the hospital and went to work in the country.

00:02:41.158 --> 00:02:44.260
The stick was a present when he left the hospital.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.072
Then, of course, he has a dog.

00:02:47.132 --> 00:02:48.493
Look at the stick.

00:02:48.553 --> 00:02:50.654
His dog carries it.

00:02:50.714 --> 00:02:52.285
I laughed.

00:02:52.345 --> 00:02:54.906
I looked in my medical dictionary.

00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:56.147
Here he is.

00:02:56.207 --> 00:02:58.057
Mortimer, James.

00:02:58.117 --> 00:02:59.058
M.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:02:59.408
R.

00:02:59.468 --> 00:02:59.538
C.

00:02:59.558 --> 00:02:59.898
S.

00:02:59.918 --> 00:03:00.528
1882.

00:03:00.588 --> 00:03:03.119
Grimpen, Dartmoor, Devon.

00:03:03.179 --> 00:03:09.051
Doctor from 1882 to 1884 at Charing Cross Hospital.

00:03:09.111 --> 00:03:10.792
See you, Watson.

00:03:10.852 --> 00:03:13.172
A hospital, not a club.

00:03:13.232 --> 00:03:14.523
But you're right.

00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:16.404
He is a country doctor.

00:03:16.464 --> 00:03:18.264
And the dog?

00:03:18.324 --> 00:03:21.127
The dog is black and white.

00:03:21.186 --> 00:03:26.072
But Holmes, please, how can you possibly know that?

00:03:26.132 --> 00:03:30.134
Well, I can see the dog outside the window.

00:03:30.194 --> 00:03:33.046
And here is Dr. Mortimer now.

00:03:33.106 --> 00:03:35.208
But what does he want?

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.390
Come in!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.953
Our visitor was tall and thin with a long nose.

00:03:42.012 --> 00:03:43.674
He wore glasses.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:49.095
He was very happy to see us, and very happy to see his stick.

00:03:49.155 --> 00:03:53.574
Thank you," he said, as Holmes gave him his stick.

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:56.855
And this was a present when I left Charing Cross Hospital.

00:03:56.915 --> 00:03:59.476
Are you Mr. Sherlock Holmes?

00:03:59.536 --> 00:04:03.347
Yes, and this is my friend Dr. Watson.

00:04:03.407 --> 00:04:05.648
I'm very pleased to meet you.

00:04:05.707 --> 00:04:07.848
You are very interesting.

00:04:07.908 --> 00:04:10.379
You have a very beautiful skull.

00:04:10.439 --> 00:04:14.082
You have an excellent Dolica Cephalic skull.

00:04:14.142 --> 00:04:16.244
Dolicoscephalic.

00:04:16.304 --> 00:04:18.505
That's a very interesting word.

00:04:18.565 --> 00:04:20.966
You know a lot about skulls.

00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:24.888
You clearly love your work, said Holmes.

00:04:24.948 --> 00:04:27.200
Please, sit down.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:30.892
So, why did you come here yesterday?

00:04:30.952 --> 00:04:33.953
Why are you here again today?

00:04:34.013 --> 00:04:37.726
You didn't come to look at my skull, I'm sure.

00:04:37.786 --> 00:04:42.469
No, I have an interesting problem and I need your help.

00:04:42.529 --> 00:04:45.370
I've got a document in my pocket."

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.202
I saw it when you came in, said Holmes.

00:04:49.262 --> 00:04:53.774
It's an old one, probably about 1730.

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:56.334
But how do you know that?

00:04:56.394 --> 00:04:59.773
You love your work and I love mine.

00:04:59.833 --> 00:05:03.895
All good detectives can look at a document and give it a date.

00:05:03.954 --> 00:05:05.015
Am I right?

00:05:05.075 --> 00:05:07.766
Two, ten or fifteen years?

00:05:07.826 --> 00:05:12.477
Yes, the date on the document is 1742.

00:05:12.537 --> 00:05:15.588
It's a Baskerville family document.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:21.170
My friend and patient Charles Baskerville gave it to me before he died.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.212
He wanted me to look after it.

00:05:23.272 --> 00:05:26.566
This document was very important to him.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.998
He was very superstitious.

00:05:29.058 --> 00:05:32.821
It's about the curse of the Baskerville family.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.443
Can I read it to you?

00:05:35.503 --> 00:05:40.086
Holmes sat back in his chair and closed his eyes.

00:05:40.146 --> 00:05:42.018
He looked bored.

00:05:42.078 --> 00:05:44.668
Dr Mortimer began.

00:05:44.728 --> 00:05:50.350
Baskerville Hall, 1742, to all Baskervilles.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:54.653
Read this story carefully, do what it says.

00:05:54.712 --> 00:06:02.358
This happened in 1647, when Hugo Baskerville lived at Baskerville Hall.

00:06:02.418 --> 00:06:05.240
He was a very bad man.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:10.044
One day, he kidnapped a young girl from her home.

00:06:10.104 --> 00:06:14.742
He took her to a room upstairs, but she escaped.

00:06:14.802 --> 00:06:19.670
She ran out of the house and ran and ran across the maw.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.992
Hugo was very angry.

00:06:22.052 --> 00:06:24.793
He followed her with his dogs.

00:06:24.853 --> 00:06:29.866
His friends followed too, but Hugo was very fast.

00:06:29.926 --> 00:06:35.258
When Hugo's friends found the girl, she was dead.

00:06:35.318 --> 00:06:40.141
They saw Hugo's dogs and they saw Hugo's body.

00:06:40.201 --> 00:06:42.276
He was dead too.

00:06:42.336 --> 00:06:48.036
His friends also saw a large black animal in the distance.

00:06:48.096 --> 00:06:49.828
It was the killer.

00:06:49.888 --> 00:06:51.360
It was a dog.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.832
But it wasn't an ordinary dog.

00:06:53.891 --> 00:06:58.706
It was a strange and terrible hound.

00:06:58.766 --> 00:07:03.562
Many of our family die in strange and terrible ways.

00:07:03.621 --> 00:07:07.346
This hound follows the Baskerville family.

00:07:07.406 --> 00:07:10.171
This is why I'm writing this story.

00:07:10.231 --> 00:07:11.833
I must tell you.

00:07:11.893 --> 00:07:16.068
Never go out on the moor at night."

00:07:16.128 --> 00:07:19.853
Dr Mortimer finished the story.

00:07:19.913 --> 00:07:25.000
Then Dr Mortimer took out a newspaper report from his pocket.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.842
Holmes looked bored again.

00:07:27.902 --> 00:07:35.235
Now, Mr. Holmes, here is something from the Dartmoor Chronicle of May the 14th this year.

00:07:35.295 --> 00:07:40.768
It's about Charles Baskerville and the story of his death.

00:07:40.828 --> 00:07:47.670
Sir, Charles Baskerville from Baskerville Hall died on May the 4th.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:53.038
He only lived here for two years, but people liked him very much.

00:07:53.098 --> 00:07:59.566
He worked in South Africa, made a lot of money, and then he returned to Devon.

00:07:59.626 --> 00:08:02.648
He helped a lot of people here.

00:08:02.708 --> 00:08:09.242
People are talking about the curse of the Baskavilles and the story of the Hound.

00:08:09.302 --> 00:08:11.403
But the facts are simple.

00:08:11.463 --> 00:08:20.678
His servants, Mr. and Mrs. Barrymore, and his doctor, Dr. James Mortimer, all say that he had a weak heart.

00:08:20.738 --> 00:08:24.028
The post-mortem showed that this was true.

00:08:24.088 --> 00:08:29.040
Barry Moore told our journalist about the night of May 4th.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:34.083
Sir Charles wanted to go to London on the morning of May 5th.

00:08:34.144 --> 00:08:36.946
After dinner he went for a walk.

00:08:37.006 --> 00:08:40.008
He always went out before bed to smoke.

00:08:40.068 --> 00:08:42.120
He didn't return.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:47.374
At twelve o'clock I was worried, so I went to look for Sir Charles.

00:08:47.434 --> 00:08:49.419
I followed his footprints.

00:08:49.479 --> 00:08:53.124
There were a lot of footprints by the gate to the moor.

00:08:53.184 --> 00:08:57.726
Then the footprints went to the end of the path.

00:08:57.786 --> 00:09:02.479
There is one strange fact from Barrymore's story.

00:09:02.539 --> 00:09:06.381
After the moor gate, the footprints were different.

00:09:06.441 --> 00:09:09.332
Sir Charles walked on Tiptoe.

00:09:09.392 --> 00:09:14.616
Sir Charles' relative, Mr. Henry Baskerville, is in Canada.

00:09:14.676 --> 00:09:19.130
All of us at the Dartmoor Chronicle hope to see him here soon.

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:23.747
We hope he can continue such as is good work.

00:09:23.807 --> 00:09:29.041
Dr. Mortimer put the newspaper back in his pocket.

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:32.654
Those facts are public, Mr. Holmes.

00:09:32.714 --> 00:09:34.726
There are other facts too.

00:09:34.786 --> 00:09:37.098
Not many people live on them all.

00:09:37.158 --> 00:09:40.180
The houses are all quite far apart.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:46.136
The only educated men are Mr. Franklin of Laughter Hall and Mr. Stapleton.

00:09:46.196 --> 00:09:47.745
He's a naturalist.

00:09:47.805 --> 00:09:51.764
But the people who live near each other spend a lot of time together.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:54.825
I spent a lot of time with Sir Charles.

00:09:54.885 --> 00:09:59.216
His stories about South Africa were very interesting.

00:09:59.276 --> 00:10:01.517
I was also his doctor.

00:10:01.577 --> 00:10:05.548
He believed in the curse of the Hound of the Bascavilles.

00:10:05.608 --> 00:10:08.124
He was terrified of it.

00:10:08.184 --> 00:10:12.303
He often heard the howl of a dog at night.

00:10:12.363 --> 00:10:15.146
One evening, I went to his house.

00:10:15.206 --> 00:10:18.728
When I arrived, I saw him at the door.

00:10:18.788 --> 00:10:20.810
His face was white.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.782
He looked terrified.

00:10:22.842 --> 00:10:27.326
I followed his eyes and saw a large black animal.

00:10:27.386 --> 00:10:30.488
It was the size of a small cow.

00:10:30.548 --> 00:10:32.480
I saw it clearly.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:37.320
It was something bad, something supernatural.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:42.280
Sir Charles' fear of the family curse was bad for him.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:46.174
I suggested a very long visit to London.

00:10:46.234 --> 00:10:48.577
He needed to rest.

00:10:48.637 --> 00:10:53.262
On the night of Sir Charles' death, Barrymore called me.

00:10:53.322 --> 00:10:56.714
I also followed the footprints down the path.

00:10:56.774 --> 00:11:00.006
I saw Barrymore's footprints too.

00:11:00.065 --> 00:11:04.688
Then, near the body, I saw other footprints.

00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:09.372
Barrymore didn't see them, but I did.

00:11:09.432 --> 00:11:14.615
Were they a man's footprints or a woman's, said Holmes?

00:11:14.675 --> 00:11:18.919
Dr. Mortimer spoke very quietly.

00:11:18.979 --> 00:11:27.167
Mr. Holmes, they were the footprints of a gigantic hound.

00:11:27.227 --> 00:11:30.990
Why didn't Barrymore see the footprints?

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:33.683
They weren't near the body.

00:11:33.743 --> 00:11:36.906
What was the weather like that night?

00:11:36.966 --> 00:11:40.114
It was cold, but it didn't rain.

00:11:40.174 --> 00:11:42.862
Can you describe the path?

00:11:42.922 --> 00:11:45.403
There are trees on each side.

00:11:45.463 --> 00:11:48.676
There is a gate on the left of the path.

00:11:48.736 --> 00:11:50.867
It goes out to the maw.

00:11:50.927 --> 00:11:56.531
So, can you only get to the path from the house or from the gate?

00:11:56.591 --> 00:11:58.962
Yes, I see.

00:11:59.022 --> 00:12:02.815
Were the footprints on the left of the path too?

00:12:02.876 --> 00:12:04.866
Yes, they were.

00:12:04.926 --> 00:12:07.109
Very interesting.

00:12:07.169 --> 00:12:10.042
And was the gate closed?

00:12:10.102 --> 00:12:12.094
And is it very high?

00:12:12.154 --> 00:12:17.038
Yes, it was closed and locked, but it's not very high.

00:12:17.098 --> 00:12:19.459
It's easy to climb over it.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:22.832
Did you see any footprints by the gate?

00:12:22.892 --> 00:12:24.764
I'm not sure.

00:12:24.824 --> 00:12:28.067
I think I only saw Sir Charles's footprints.

00:12:28.127 --> 00:12:29.878
There were a lot of them.

00:12:29.938 --> 00:12:32.770
I know he was there for about ten minutes.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.918
How do you know that?

00:12:34.978 --> 00:12:38.407
There was a match and part of a cigarette.

00:12:38.467 --> 00:12:41.050
He spoke to cigarette there.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:42.811
Excellent.

00:12:42.871 --> 00:12:44.052
Congratulations.

00:12:44.112 --> 00:12:46.124
You're a detective too.

00:12:46.184 --> 00:12:51.104
So, you want me to investigate Sir Charles' death?

00:12:51.164 --> 00:12:52.540
Not really.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.821
I think Sir Charles died of fright.

00:12:54.881 --> 00:12:57.772
My problem is with Sir Henry Baskerville.

00:12:57.832 --> 00:13:01.024
He arrives at Waterloo station at one o'clock today.

00:13:01.084 --> 00:13:04.175
He's the only heir to Baskerville Hall.

00:13:04.235 --> 00:13:06.866
I think he wants to go to the hall.

00:13:06.926 --> 00:13:09.948
But I don't think the hall is safe for him.

00:13:10.008 --> 00:13:12.322
I don't know what to do.

00:13:12.382 --> 00:13:15.056
Go to Waterloo station.

00:13:15.116 --> 00:13:18.427
Meet Henry Baskerville and take him to his hotel.

00:13:18.487 --> 00:13:20.798
I need time to think about this.

00:13:20.858 --> 00:13:23.449
Come here tomorrow at 10 o'clock.

00:13:23.509 --> 00:13:25.430
Brings a Henry with you.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:28.791
But before you go, one more question.

00:13:28.852 --> 00:13:34.914
Before Sir Charles's death, how many people saw this hound on the moor?

00:13:34.974 --> 00:13:37.295
Three people saw it.

00:13:37.355 --> 00:13:40.546
Did anyone see it after Sir Charles died?

00:13:40.566 --> 00:13:42.266
No.

00:13:42.326 --> 00:13:45.356
Thank you, Dr. Mortimer.

00:13:45.416 --> 00:13:47.458
A good morning.

00:13:47.518 --> 00:13:50.640
Holmes returned to his chair.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.672
He looked pleased about this new case.

00:13:53.732 --> 00:13:55.834
I need time alone.

00:13:55.894 --> 00:13:57.646
I need to think, Watson.

00:13:57.706 --> 00:14:00.078
Can you go out until this evening?

00:14:00.138 --> 00:14:03.120
Then we can talk about this case together.

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:06.243
I spent the day at my club.

00:14:06.302 --> 00:14:09.496
I returned at about nine o'clock.

00:14:09.556 --> 00:14:13.808
So, you went to your club for the day.

00:14:13.868 --> 00:14:16.338
Yes, but how?

00:14:16.398 --> 00:14:18.460
He laughed.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.372
Elementary, Watson.

00:14:21.432 --> 00:14:24.355
It rained all morning and all afternoon.

00:14:24.415 --> 00:14:26.276
You're completely dry.

00:14:26.336 --> 00:14:29.038
Look, your hat and your shoes are dry.

00:14:29.098 --> 00:14:32.302
So it's clear that you spent the day inside.

00:14:32.362 --> 00:14:37.502
As for me, I studied this map of Dartmoor all afternoon.

00:14:37.562 --> 00:14:41.290
He put the map on the table and showed me.

00:14:41.349 --> 00:14:44.140
This is Baskerville Hall.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:46.602
Can you see the trees around it?

00:14:46.662 --> 00:14:50.333
And this is the path where Sir Charles died.

00:14:50.393 --> 00:14:53.774
This is the village of Grimpen.

00:14:53.834 --> 00:14:56.476
That's where Dr. Mortimer lives.

00:14:56.536 --> 00:14:58.467
Here is laughter hall.

00:14:58.527 --> 00:15:00.358
Mr. Franklin lives there.

00:15:00.418 --> 00:15:03.739
And this is probably Mr. Stapleton's house.

00:15:03.799 --> 00:15:07.226
You can see that they are all quite far apart.

00:15:07.286 --> 00:15:10.834
Over here, there are some farmhouses.

00:15:10.894 --> 00:15:14.875
Then here, 14 miles away, is Princeton Prison.

00:15:14.935 --> 00:15:18.056
All around, there's the moor.

00:15:18.116 --> 00:15:21.007
It's a lonely place.

00:15:21.067 --> 00:15:23.978
Do you think Dr Mortimer is right, Holmes?

00:15:24.038 --> 00:15:27.709
Do you think the Hound is a supernatural animal?

00:15:27.769 --> 00:15:30.982
And Dr Mortimer thinks that it's supernatural?

00:15:31.041 --> 00:15:33.805
He believes the family curse.

00:15:33.866 --> 00:15:37.148
I believe in facts, Watson, not stories.

00:15:37.208 --> 00:15:40.812
Our first job is to look for the facts.

00:15:40.872 --> 00:15:44.674
Did Sir Charles die because of his heart?

00:15:44.734 --> 00:15:47.647
Or did someone kill him?

00:15:47.707 --> 00:15:53.995
Chapter 2 The letter, the shoes, and the man with the beard.

00:15:54.055 --> 00:15:58.940
Well, Watson, you know the results of my work today.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.590
What about you?

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:03.052
Did you think about our new case?

00:16:03.112 --> 00:16:04.692
Said Holmes.

00:16:04.752 --> 00:16:06.143
Yes, I did.

00:16:06.163 --> 00:16:08.354
I thought a lot about it.

00:16:08.414 --> 00:16:11.616
There are some things I don't understand.

00:16:11.676 --> 00:16:15.177
Why did Sir Charles' footprints change?

00:16:15.237 --> 00:16:18.108
Why did he walk on Tiptoe?

00:16:18.168 --> 00:16:19.729
He didn't.

00:16:19.789 --> 00:16:21.153
He ran.

00:16:21.213 --> 00:16:24.027
When you run, your footprints change.

00:16:24.087 --> 00:16:26.398
Sir Charles ran Watson.

00:16:26.458 --> 00:16:28.409
He ran for his life.

00:16:28.469 --> 00:16:30.531
He was terrified.

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:34.012
But what did he run away from?

00:16:34.072 --> 00:16:36.713
Now that's the problem.

00:16:36.773 --> 00:16:38.244
It's strange.

00:16:38.304 --> 00:16:41.185
He didn't run in the direction of the house.

00:16:41.245 --> 00:16:42.976
He ran away from it.

00:16:43.036 --> 00:16:45.107
Help, was that the house?

00:16:45.167 --> 00:16:47.379
But he ran away.

00:16:47.439 --> 00:16:50.632
And why did he wait at the gate?

00:16:50.692 --> 00:16:52.944
Did he want to meet someone?

00:16:53.004 --> 00:16:55.936
Sir Charles was old and quite ill.

00:16:55.996 --> 00:16:57.808
It was a cold night.

00:16:57.868 --> 00:17:02.112
It seems strange that he stopped for a long time by the gate.

00:17:02.172 --> 00:17:06.746
Remember, a doctor Mortimer told us about the match and the cigarette.

00:17:06.805 --> 00:17:09.868
He had time to smoke a cigarette there.

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:13.612
Ten minutes is a long time for an ill man.

00:17:13.671 --> 00:17:16.143
But he went out every evening.

00:17:16.203 --> 00:17:21.034
Yes, but I'm sure he didn't wait by the more gate every evening.

00:17:21.095 --> 00:17:23.686
He was afraid of the more.

00:17:23.746 --> 00:17:26.496
But that night he waited there.

00:17:26.557 --> 00:17:29.388
It was the night before his trip to London.

00:17:29.448 --> 00:17:33.079
Ah, Watson, I think I'm beginning to understand something.

00:17:33.139 --> 00:17:35.330
Pass me my vial in my friend.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:39.978
Let's wait until our meeting with Sir Henry Baskerville in the morning.

00:17:40.038 --> 00:17:44.336
Our visitors arrived at exactly ten o'clock.

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:48.748
Sir Henry Baskerville was a small man with dark eyes.

00:17:48.808 --> 00:17:52.970
He was about thirty years old and was strong and healthy.

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:59.484
He was a gentleman, but it was also clear that he liked spending time outside.

00:17:59.544 --> 00:18:02.245
I'm very pleased to meet you, Mr. Holmes.

00:18:02.305 --> 00:18:04.156
Can I show you something?

00:18:04.216 --> 00:18:05.916
It's a strange letter.

00:18:05.976 --> 00:18:08.049
I got it this morning.

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:11.652
Sir Henry put the letter on the table.

00:18:11.712 --> 00:18:17.134
The address said Sir Henry Baskerville Northumberland Hotel.

00:18:17.194 --> 00:18:19.514
That's very interesting.

00:18:19.574 --> 00:18:23.145
Did anyone know you were at the Northumberland Hotel?

00:18:23.205 --> 00:18:24.945
Said Holmes.

00:18:25.005 --> 00:18:30.456
No, Dr. Mortimer and I only decided when I arrived at the station.

00:18:30.516 --> 00:18:34.350
Hmm, someone followed you.

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:37.082
Holmes looked at the letter.

00:18:37.142 --> 00:18:39.373
There was only one sentence.

00:18:39.433 --> 00:18:43.344
Almost all the words were from a newspaper.

00:18:43.404 --> 00:18:46.534
You are in danger.

00:18:46.594 --> 00:18:50.185
Keep away from the more.

00:18:50.245 --> 00:18:55.566
Only the word more wasn't from the newspaper.

00:18:55.626 --> 00:18:58.067
Very interesting.

00:18:58.127 --> 00:19:01.098
Have you got yesterday's times, Watson?

00:19:01.158 --> 00:19:03.959
I gave the newspaper to him.

00:19:04.019 --> 00:19:05.582
Yes.

00:19:05.642 --> 00:19:07.194
Here, can you see?

00:19:07.254 --> 00:19:09.738
These words are all on the front page.

00:19:09.798 --> 00:19:13.474
The words in this letter come from the times.

00:19:13.534 --> 00:19:17.309
Dr Mortimer was very surprised.

00:19:17.369 --> 00:19:20.983
But how did you know which newspaper to look at?

00:19:21.043 --> 00:19:25.694
Well, as I said yesterday, we both love our work.

00:19:25.754 --> 00:19:29.788
You know all about skulls because it's your special hobby.

00:19:29.848 --> 00:19:32.059
This is my special hobby.

00:19:32.119 --> 00:19:34.410
Most newspapers have a style.

00:19:34.471 --> 00:19:38.142
The Times front page is very obvious.

00:19:38.202 --> 00:19:42.676
So someone cut out this message, said Sir Henry.

00:19:42.736 --> 00:19:45.898
But why did he write the word more?

00:19:45.958 --> 00:19:48.912
Because it wasn't in the newspaper.

00:19:48.972 --> 00:19:51.556
The word more is unusual.

00:19:51.616 --> 00:19:53.518
That's why he wrote it.

00:19:53.578 --> 00:19:57.960
And another thing, the address is in bad writing.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:02.484
But people who read the times are usually educated people.

00:20:02.544 --> 00:20:08.668
Our writer is an educated man, but he wants to seem uneducated.

00:20:08.728 --> 00:20:12.990
Why does he want to hide his writing from you, Sir Henry?

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:15.984
Does he think you know his writing?

00:20:16.044 --> 00:20:21.736
And another thing, I also think our man wrote this in a hotel.

00:20:21.796 --> 00:20:24.688
How can you possibly know that?

00:20:24.748 --> 00:20:27.108
Said Dr Mortimer.

00:20:27.168 --> 00:20:31.090
You can see that the writer didn't know the pen.

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:34.731
The pen and the ink gave our writer some problems.

00:20:34.791 --> 00:20:37.302
That's why I think he was in a hotel.

00:20:37.362 --> 00:20:38.440
Yes.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:42.230
Watson, we must look in the hotels near Charing Cross.

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:44.912
Somewhere near there there's a bin.

00:20:44.972 --> 00:20:47.624
In it there's a copy of the Times.

00:20:47.684 --> 00:20:50.326
The words in this letter are missing from it.

00:20:50.386 --> 00:20:53.558
Sir Henry, did anyone follow you yesterday?

00:20:53.618 --> 00:20:55.318
I didn't see anyone.

00:20:55.378 --> 00:20:57.430
But a strange thing happened.

00:20:57.490 --> 00:20:59.131
I lost a shoe.

00:20:59.191 --> 00:21:00.892
They were new shoes.

00:21:00.952 --> 00:21:03.034
I bought them yesterday afternoon.

00:21:03.094 --> 00:21:04.904
I put them in my wardrobe.

00:21:04.964 --> 00:21:09.344
This morning there was only one shoe there.

00:21:09.404 --> 00:21:13.602
But why did anybody steal a shoe?

00:21:13.662 --> 00:21:15.563
And why one shoe?"

00:21:15.623 --> 00:21:16.874
I said.

00:21:16.934 --> 00:21:19.475
I know, said Sir Henry.

00:21:19.535 --> 00:21:20.846
It's very strange.

00:21:20.906 --> 00:21:23.037
But now you must tell me.

00:21:23.097 --> 00:21:24.518
Why am I here?

00:21:24.578 --> 00:21:26.650
What's happening?

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:30.022
Tell him, said Holmes.

00:21:30.082 --> 00:21:37.086
Dr. Mortimer read the Baskerville family document and the newspaper report to Sir Henry.

00:21:37.146 --> 00:21:40.199
Well, said Sir Henry.

00:21:40.259 --> 00:21:43.982
Strange things are happening at Baskerville Hall.

00:21:44.042 --> 00:21:46.964
And now there's this strange letter.

00:21:47.024 --> 00:21:49.757
Does someone want to stop me from going to the hall?

00:21:49.777 --> 00:21:53.610
I don't know, said Dr Mortimer.

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:56.092
Perhaps someone knows the more is dangerous.

00:21:56.152 --> 00:21:58.934
Perhaps he wants to help you.

00:21:58.994 --> 00:22:01.426
Holmes stood up.

00:22:01.486 --> 00:22:03.378
That's the problem.

00:22:03.438 --> 00:22:06.266
Is Baskerville Hall safe?

00:22:06.326 --> 00:22:11.566
Well, I want to go to my family home, said Sir Henry.

00:22:11.626 --> 00:22:13.758
No one can stop me.

00:22:13.818 --> 00:22:16.170
I need time to think.

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:18.452
Come to my hotel at two o'clock.

00:22:18.512 --> 00:22:21.424
Then I can tell you what I want to do.

00:22:21.484 --> 00:22:27.438
Dr. Mortimer and Henry Baskerville left our house in Baker Street.

00:22:27.498 --> 00:22:30.521
Suddenly, homes jumped up.

00:22:30.581 --> 00:22:33.394
Quick Watson, let's follow them.

00:22:33.454 --> 00:22:35.796
We ran outside.

00:22:35.856 --> 00:22:39.419
We saw them about a hundred yards away.

00:22:39.479 --> 00:22:43.941
They walked into Oxford Street and then into Regent Street.

00:22:44.001 --> 00:22:46.972
They stopped and looked in a shop window.

00:22:47.032 --> 00:22:50.123
A cab opposite stopped too.

00:22:50.183 --> 00:22:52.834
That cab's following them Watson.

00:22:52.894 --> 00:22:55.334
Quick, let's see who's in it.

00:22:55.394 --> 00:23:00.236
In the cab, I could see a man with a big black beard.

00:23:00.297 --> 00:23:04.438
But the man saw us and the cab drove quickly away.

00:23:04.498 --> 00:23:08.570
Holmes chased it, but the cab was too fast.

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:11.662
It was cab 2704.

00:23:11.722 --> 00:23:13.784
Did you see the man, Watson?

00:23:13.844 --> 00:23:16.454
Yes, he had a beard.

00:23:16.514 --> 00:23:20.186
I followed Holmes into an office building.

00:23:20.246 --> 00:23:22.738
Where's Cartwright, the message boy?

00:23:22.798 --> 00:23:24.098
Ah, there he is.

00:23:24.158 --> 00:23:26.010
Cartwright, come here, boy.

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:28.250
Bring me a hotel directory.

00:23:28.310 --> 00:23:31.218
The boy ran quickly to Holmes.

00:23:31.278 --> 00:23:37.388
Now, Cartwright, here are the names of 23 hotels near Charing Cross.

00:23:37.448 --> 00:23:39.149
Visit them all.

00:23:39.209 --> 00:23:43.142
Tell the porters that you want to see the bins from yesterday.

00:23:43.202 --> 00:23:46.876
Tell them that a client lost an important telegram.

00:23:46.936 --> 00:23:48.426
Do you understand?

00:23:48.486 --> 00:23:50.038
Yes, sir.

00:23:50.098 --> 00:23:53.646
Cartwright was an intelligent boy.

00:23:53.706 --> 00:23:58.712
But you're really looking for a copy of yesterday's times.

00:23:58.772 --> 00:24:02.624
You're looking for a copy with some words missing.

00:24:02.683 --> 00:24:05.154
Go now, and good luck.

00:24:05.214 --> 00:24:08.016
Now Watson, let's go to the cab office.

00:24:08.076 --> 00:24:12.397
I want to leave a message for the driver of cab number 2704.

00:24:12.457 --> 00:24:16.148
Then let's go to Sir Henry's hotel.

00:24:16.208 --> 00:24:22.272
Sir Henry Baskerville is waiting for you, said the hotel receptionist.

00:24:22.332 --> 00:24:24.386
We went upstairs.

00:24:24.446 --> 00:24:26.298
Sir Henry was there.

00:24:26.358 --> 00:24:28.510
He was very angry.

00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:30.451
Another shoe!

00:24:30.511 --> 00:24:31.612
He shouted.

00:24:31.672 --> 00:24:34.384
Why is someone stealing my shoes?

00:24:34.444 --> 00:24:37.376
Yesterday they stole one of my new brown shoes.

00:24:37.436 --> 00:24:41.400
This morning they stole one of my old black shoes.

00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:45.042
How strange, said Holmes.

00:24:45.102 --> 00:24:50.493
We went into Sir Henry's sitting room and we talked about his plans.

00:24:50.553 --> 00:24:56.104
Now, Sir Henry, what do you want to do, said Holmes?

00:24:56.164 --> 00:25:00.556
I want to go to Baskerville Hall at the end of this week.

00:25:00.616 --> 00:25:03.008
I think it's a good idea.

00:25:03.068 --> 00:25:05.730
You're in danger in London.

00:25:05.790 --> 00:25:08.782
This morning someone followed you.

00:25:08.842 --> 00:25:12.455
Dr. Mortimer was very surprised.

00:25:12.515 --> 00:25:14.256
We didn't see anyone.

00:25:14.316 --> 00:25:16.508
Did you see the person?

00:25:16.568 --> 00:25:18.480
No, I didn't.

00:25:18.540 --> 00:25:21.266
But he had a big black beard.

00:25:21.327 --> 00:25:26.604
Do you know anyone on Dartmoor with a big black beard?

00:25:26.664 --> 00:25:28.494
Barrymore!

00:25:28.554 --> 00:25:30.285
He's such as his butler!

00:25:30.345 --> 00:25:32.236
He's got a big black beard!

00:25:32.296 --> 00:25:35.076
But he's at Baskerville Hall!

00:25:35.136 --> 00:25:36.497
Are you sure?

00:25:36.517 --> 00:25:38.198
Let's check.

00:25:38.258 --> 00:25:41.669
So Henry, you must send telegram to Barrymore.

00:25:41.729 --> 00:25:45.716
Say, is everything ready for my arrival?

00:25:45.777 --> 00:25:51.126
Say that the telegram must go to Barrymore and only Barrymore.

00:25:51.186 --> 00:25:53.308
Ask him to send you an answer.

00:25:53.368 --> 00:25:59.402
Now, Dr Mortimer, did Sir Charles leave the Barrymore's any money in his will?

00:25:59.462 --> 00:26:03.034
Yes, he left them £500.

00:26:03.094 --> 00:26:06.942
Did they know about this before Sir Charles died?

00:26:07.002 --> 00:26:08.519
Yes, they did.

00:26:08.579 --> 00:26:11.450
Sir Charles often talked about his will.

00:26:11.510 --> 00:26:14.983
Sir Charles gave a lot of money to a lot of people.

00:26:15.043 --> 00:26:17.896
He was a very kind man.

00:26:17.956 --> 00:26:23.018
When Sir Charles died, he had nearly a million pounds.

00:26:23.078 --> 00:26:27.021
Now, Sir Henry has a lot of money.

00:26:27.082 --> 00:26:29.644
Very rich.

00:26:29.704 --> 00:26:32.014
Very interesting.

00:26:32.074 --> 00:26:35.762
And who is Sir Henry's heir?

00:26:35.822 --> 00:26:40.167
Sir Charles' second brother died when he was young.

00:26:40.227 --> 00:26:43.258
Sir Henry here is his son.

00:26:43.318 --> 00:26:47.179
Roger Baskerville was Sir Charles' third brother.

00:26:47.239 --> 00:26:50.200
He was a dangerous man, like Hugo.

00:26:50.260 --> 00:26:55.101
He had problems with the police, so he went to Central America.

00:26:55.161 --> 00:26:56.961
He died there.

00:26:57.021 --> 00:26:59.662
He didn't marry before he died.

00:26:59.722 --> 00:27:04.999
Sir Charles' brothers are dead, so Sir Henry is the only heir.

00:27:05.059 --> 00:27:06.966
I see.

00:27:07.026 --> 00:27:13.210
Well, Sir Henry, you can go to Baskerville Hall, but not alone.

00:27:13.270 --> 00:27:17.894
I'm investigating something for a famous person, so I can't come myself.

00:27:17.954 --> 00:27:19.966
Oh, Watson, you must go.

00:27:20.026 --> 00:27:22.798
Yes, of course, I said.

00:27:22.858 --> 00:27:25.880
We walked towards the door.

00:27:25.941 --> 00:27:30.404
Suddenly, Sir Henry shouted, I'm you, sure.

00:27:30.464 --> 00:27:33.252
There it is, under that chair.

00:27:33.312 --> 00:27:37.012
strange," said Dr. Mortimer.

00:27:37.072 --> 00:27:40.256
We searched this room very carefully before lunch.

00:27:40.316 --> 00:27:43.128
There wasn't a shoe here then.

00:27:43.188 --> 00:27:46.100
Holmes and I went home.

00:27:46.160 --> 00:27:50.104
In the cab I thought about the last two days.

00:27:50.164 --> 00:27:53.147
First there was the strange letter.

00:27:53.207 --> 00:27:56.010
Then the man with the black beard.

00:27:56.070 --> 00:28:00.273
Then the missing brown shoe and the missing black shoe.

00:28:00.333 --> 00:28:03.885
Now the return of the brown shoe.

00:28:03.945 --> 00:28:06.656
What did these things mean?

00:28:06.716 --> 00:28:10.509
Just before dinner, two telegrams arrived.

00:28:10.569 --> 00:28:12.600
One was from Sir Henry.

00:28:12.660 --> 00:28:16.972
Barrymore is at Baskerville Hall, not in London.

00:28:17.032 --> 00:28:19.774
The other was from Cartwright.

00:28:19.834 --> 00:28:22.756
I visited 23 hotels today.

00:28:22.816 --> 00:28:25.618
Sorry, no times.

00:28:25.678 --> 00:28:28.470
Oh, well, said Holmes.

00:28:28.530 --> 00:28:30.280
No luck there, then.

00:28:30.340 --> 00:28:32.551
But I like difficult cases.

00:28:32.611 --> 00:28:35.832
Now, who's that at the door?

00:28:35.893 --> 00:28:38.353
A man came into the room.

00:28:38.413 --> 00:28:39.634
Good evening.

00:28:39.694 --> 00:28:41.214
I got your message.

00:28:41.274 --> 00:28:44.255
I'm the driver of CAP2704.

00:28:44.315 --> 00:28:46.996
Thank you for coming, said Holmes.

00:28:47.056 --> 00:28:49.627
I want to ask you some questions.

00:28:49.687 --> 00:28:52.028
What do you want to know?

00:28:52.088 --> 00:28:55.510
Tell me about your passenger this morning.

00:28:55.570 --> 00:29:00.426
He watched this house, and then he followed two gentlemen.

00:29:00.486 --> 00:29:03.168
The cab driver was surprised.

00:29:03.228 --> 00:29:04.539
Yes, he did.

00:29:04.559 --> 00:29:07.300
He knew a lot already.

00:29:07.360 --> 00:29:09.992
But the gentleman was a detective.

00:29:10.052 --> 00:29:12.144
He told me his name.

00:29:12.204 --> 00:29:15.316
Holmes looked at me and smiled.

00:29:15.376 --> 00:29:16.948
Excellent.

00:29:17.008 --> 00:29:19.140
What was his name?

00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:22.476
His name, said the cab driver.

00:29:22.536 --> 00:29:26.120
was Mr. Sherlock Holmes.

00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:33.232
We were both very surprised, but Holmes continued, excellent again.

00:29:33.292 --> 00:29:36.712
Now, tell me, where did you go?

00:29:36.772 --> 00:29:41.003
He stopped me at half past nine in Trafalgar Square.

00:29:41.063 --> 00:29:43.944
Then we went to the Northumberland Hotel.

00:29:44.004 --> 00:29:45.874
Two gentlemen came out.

00:29:45.934 --> 00:29:47.354
They took a cab.

00:29:47.414 --> 00:29:48.904
We followed it.

00:29:48.964 --> 00:29:51.846
It stopped in Baker Street near here.

00:29:51.906 --> 00:29:54.580
We waited for about an hour and a half.

00:29:54.640 --> 00:29:56.300
Then they came out.

00:29:56.360 --> 00:29:58.172
We followed them.

00:29:58.232 --> 00:30:05.797
Then, suddenly in Regent Street, my passenger said, quick, take me to my hotel.

00:30:05.857 --> 00:30:08.118
So that's what I did.

00:30:08.178 --> 00:30:09.950
I see.

00:30:10.010 --> 00:30:14.442
And can you describe Mr Sherlock Holmes?

00:30:14.502 --> 00:30:17.645
He was about 40 years old.

00:30:17.705 --> 00:30:20.724
He had a black beard and a pale face.

00:30:20.784 --> 00:30:22.181
It was quite tall.

00:30:22.201 --> 00:30:24.602
A bit like you, sir."

00:30:24.662 --> 00:30:26.562
Thank you very much.

00:30:26.622 --> 00:30:28.812
Here's some money for you.

00:30:28.872 --> 00:30:31.513
The cab driver went away.

00:30:31.573 --> 00:30:34.724
He looked very, very pleased.

00:30:34.784 --> 00:30:38.584
No luck there, either, said Holmes.

00:30:38.644 --> 00:30:42.265
Watson, this is a dangerous case.

00:30:42.325 --> 00:30:45.226
I'm worried about your visit to Dartmoor.

00:30:45.286 --> 00:30:48.406
I need you to go to Baskerville Hall.

00:30:48.466 --> 00:30:51.868
But you must be very careful.

00:30:51.928 --> 00:31:03.435
Chapter 3 The Prisoner on the More On Saturday we met Baskerville and Mortimer at the station.

00:31:03.496 --> 00:31:06.958
Did you have a good week, said Holmes?

00:31:07.018 --> 00:31:09.269
Did anyone follow you?

00:31:09.330 --> 00:31:13.992
No, no one followed us, said Dr. Mortimer.

00:31:14.052 --> 00:31:17.724
And did you find your shoes, Henry?

00:31:17.784 --> 00:31:19.835
No, I didn't.

00:31:19.895 --> 00:31:22.068
Very interesting.

00:31:22.128 --> 00:31:29.492
Well, be careful at the hall and don't go on to the moor alone at night.

00:31:29.552 --> 00:31:32.542
Holmes then looked at me.

00:31:32.602 --> 00:31:38.054
Write reports to me, Watson, but I only want the facts.

00:31:38.114 --> 00:31:42.905
Tell me about Sir Henry's neighbours and about Sir Charles's death.

00:31:42.966 --> 00:31:45.796
Study the people on the moor.

00:31:45.856 --> 00:31:47.677
Yes, of course.

00:31:47.737 --> 00:31:49.597
I see you've got your gun.

00:31:49.657 --> 00:31:50.398
Good.

00:31:50.458 --> 00:31:52.323
Always have it with you.

00:31:52.383 --> 00:31:56.622
Goodbye, and good luck, my friend.

00:31:56.682 --> 00:31:59.434
I got onto the train.

00:31:59.494 --> 00:32:03.018
It was a long journey, but I enjoyed it.

00:32:03.078 --> 00:32:09.524
I talked to Sir Henry and Dr Mortimer, and I played with the doctor's friendly dog.

00:32:09.584 --> 00:32:12.438
Sir Henry looked out of the window.

00:32:12.498 --> 00:32:16.191
He was very interested in the countryside.

00:32:16.251 --> 00:32:19.752
I don't know what Baskerville Hall is like.

00:32:19.812 --> 00:32:23.063
I was only a teenager when my father died.

00:32:23.123 --> 00:32:28.824
We lived in a little house on the south coast, and I never visited the hall.

00:32:28.884 --> 00:32:32.505
Then, after my father died, I went to Canada.

00:32:32.565 --> 00:32:37.626
I can't wait to see the hall, and I can't wait to see the more."

00:32:37.686 --> 00:32:42.276
Well, there's the more," said Dr. Mortimer.

00:32:42.336 --> 00:32:45.496
Sir Henry looked out of the window.

00:32:45.557 --> 00:32:47.908
There was the moor.

00:32:47.968 --> 00:32:49.810
He was silent.

00:32:49.870 --> 00:32:52.112
This was his new home.

00:32:52.172 --> 00:32:54.784
I saw he loved it.

00:32:54.844 --> 00:32:58.386
The train stopped at a small station.

00:32:58.446 --> 00:33:02.710
Outside the station, we saw a carriage with two horses.

00:33:02.770 --> 00:33:06.172
There were also two soldiers with guns.

00:33:06.232 --> 00:33:08.223
It was strange.

00:33:08.284 --> 00:33:11.398
Why were their soldiers here?

00:33:11.458 --> 00:33:16.614
Perkins, our driver, took us quickly to Baskerville Hall.

00:33:16.674 --> 00:33:21.228
Sir Henry asked lots of questions about the hall and the moor.

00:33:21.288 --> 00:33:25.652
He was like a little boy excited about his new home.

00:33:25.712 --> 00:33:30.125
Then, in the distance, we saw a soldier on the hill.

00:33:30.186 --> 00:33:33.618
He was on a horse, and he had a gun.

00:33:33.678 --> 00:33:37.001
He watched our carriage as we passed.

00:33:37.062 --> 00:33:39.664
What's this about, Perkins?

00:33:39.724 --> 00:33:41.501
Said Dr. Mortimer.

00:33:41.561 --> 00:33:43.918
There's a prisoner on the moor.

00:33:43.978 --> 00:33:46.970
He escaped from Princeton Prison three days ago.

00:33:47.030 --> 00:33:50.552
The soldiers are watching all the roads and train stations.

00:33:50.612 --> 00:33:52.963
People are afraid, sir.

00:33:53.024 --> 00:33:55.604
Who is this prisoner?

00:33:55.664 --> 00:34:00.608
It's Selden, the Notting Hill Killer.

00:34:00.668 --> 00:34:04.180
Everyone in the carriage was silent.

00:34:04.240 --> 00:34:11.691
Then, at last, in the distance, we saw them, the two towers of Baskerville Hall.

00:34:11.750 --> 00:34:14.870
Sir Henry looked at the house.

00:34:14.930 --> 00:34:18.514
It doesn't look very friendly, he said.

00:34:18.574 --> 00:34:20.666
Then he smiled.

00:34:20.726 --> 00:34:23.118
I think it needs more light.

00:34:23.178 --> 00:34:24.279
Yes.

00:34:24.339 --> 00:34:26.811
Electric light before next year.

00:34:26.872 --> 00:34:28.783
That's what we need.

00:34:28.843 --> 00:34:31.656
A tall man was at the door.

00:34:31.716 --> 00:34:33.748
A woman was with him.

00:34:33.808 --> 00:34:35.930
Welcome, Sir Henry.

00:34:35.990 --> 00:34:39.097
Welcome to Baskerville Hall.

00:34:39.157 --> 00:34:43.514
This was Barrymore, the butler, and his wife.

00:34:43.574 --> 00:34:46.766
They took our bags, and we followed them inside.

00:34:46.786 --> 00:34:50.038
"'Well, Sir Henry, I must go.

00:34:50.098 --> 00:34:53.170
My wife's waiting,' said Dr. Mortimer.

00:34:53.190 --> 00:34:55.871
"'Have some dinner before you go.

00:34:55.891 --> 00:34:58.593
Nio, I must go home.

00:34:58.653 --> 00:35:01.859
But please call me any time, night or day.'

00:35:01.919 --> 00:35:03.854
Thank you, Dr. Mortimer.

00:35:03.914 --> 00:35:05.596
You're a good friend.

00:35:05.656 --> 00:35:08.439
Now, Barrymore, show us to our rooms.

00:35:08.499 --> 00:35:10.141
Is there any hot water?

00:35:10.201 --> 00:35:11.772
Can I have a wash?

00:35:11.832 --> 00:35:13.154
Yes, sir.

00:35:13.214 --> 00:35:15.776
There's hot water in your rooms.

00:35:15.836 --> 00:35:17.658
Thank you, Barrymore.

00:35:17.718 --> 00:35:20.908
But do you have something to say?

00:35:20.968 --> 00:35:22.806
Yes, sir.

00:35:22.866 --> 00:35:27.217
I'm sorry, but my wife and I want to leave here.

00:35:27.278 --> 00:35:32.850
We liked Sir Charles very much, and he gave us a lot of money in his will.

00:35:32.910 --> 00:35:36.261
The hall is a sad place for us now.

00:35:36.321 --> 00:35:38.802
Do you want to leave immediately?

00:35:38.862 --> 00:35:40.063
No, no.

00:35:40.123 --> 00:35:41.393
We can wait.

00:35:41.453 --> 00:35:43.714
Find a new butler first.

00:35:43.774 --> 00:35:45.615
Then we can leave.

00:35:45.675 --> 00:35:49.149
Can I show you your rooms now, sir?

00:35:49.209 --> 00:35:52.434
We followed Barrymore upstairs.

00:35:52.494 --> 00:35:55.455
My room was near Sir Henry's.

00:35:55.515 --> 00:35:58.006
It was almost next to it.

00:35:58.067 --> 00:36:01.448
These rooms were light and cheerful.

00:36:01.508 --> 00:36:05.140
The rest of the house was old and dark.

00:36:05.200 --> 00:36:09.142
I had a wash and changed my clothes for dinner.

00:36:09.202 --> 00:36:13.942
Then I went into the dining room where I met Sir Henry.

00:36:14.002 --> 00:36:19.241
It was a very large room, but it was also old and dark.

00:36:19.301 --> 00:36:23.252
Pictures of the Baskerville family were on the walls.

00:36:23.312 --> 00:36:26.364
They looked at us while we had our dinner.

00:36:26.424 --> 00:36:29.035
We both felt uncomfortable there.

00:36:29.095 --> 00:36:31.106
We didn't talk a lot at dinner.

00:36:31.126 --> 00:36:37.788
"'I'm not surprised my uncle was a nervous man,' said Sir Henry.

00:36:37.848 --> 00:36:42.420
He was all alone in this big dark house.

00:36:42.480 --> 00:36:47.752
After dinner we said good night and went to our rooms.

00:36:47.812 --> 00:36:50.363
I looked out of the window.

00:36:50.423 --> 00:36:53.804
I could see the garden in the moonlight.

00:36:53.864 --> 00:36:58.617
In the distance there was the dark lonely moor.

00:36:58.677 --> 00:37:02.128
I closed the curtains and went to bed.

00:37:02.188 --> 00:37:04.810
It was difficult to sleep.

00:37:04.870 --> 00:37:07.461
The house was silent.

00:37:07.521 --> 00:37:12.278
Then suddenly in the middle of the night I heard something.

00:37:12.339 --> 00:37:15.638
I sat up in bed and listened carefully.

00:37:15.698 --> 00:37:21.045
It wasn't far away, and it was certainly in the house.

00:37:21.106 --> 00:37:27.975
Someone's crying, I said to myself, it's a woman, and she's crying.

00:37:28.035 --> 00:37:31.654
Now, why?

00:37:31.714 --> 00:37:35.912
The next morning was beautiful.

00:37:35.972 --> 00:37:39.746
And breakfast the sunlight filled the room.

00:37:39.806 --> 00:37:42.848
It was very different from the night before.

00:37:42.908 --> 00:37:46.411
We talked happily over breakfast.

00:37:46.471 --> 00:37:49.784
Perhaps we were tired last night.

00:37:49.844 --> 00:37:52.196
That's why this place looked sad.

00:37:52.256 --> 00:37:55.168
It was probably our imagination.

00:37:55.228 --> 00:37:57.858
Now it seems very cheerful.

00:37:57.918 --> 00:38:00.357
Yes, I answered.

00:38:00.417 --> 00:38:03.649
But did you hear anything last night?

00:38:03.709 --> 00:38:05.390
Did you hear a woman?

00:38:05.450 --> 00:38:07.211
Yes, I did.

00:38:07.271 --> 00:38:09.462
And she was very unhappy.

00:38:09.522 --> 00:38:12.024
She cried and cried.

00:38:12.084 --> 00:38:14.716
But I thought it was a dream.

00:38:14.776 --> 00:38:17.687
Well, it wasn't a dream.

00:38:17.747 --> 00:38:20.152
I heard it too.

00:38:20.212 --> 00:38:23.616
Sir Henry called Barrymore.

00:38:23.676 --> 00:38:26.378
He asked him about the woman.

00:38:26.438 --> 00:38:30.240
Barrymore's face went a little pale.

00:38:30.300 --> 00:38:34.152
There are only two women in the house, Sir Henry.

00:38:34.212 --> 00:38:38.825
One is the maid, and she sleeps in the other part of the house.

00:38:38.885 --> 00:38:41.626
The other woman is my wife.

00:38:41.687 --> 00:38:45.324
The sound did not come from her.

00:38:45.384 --> 00:38:50.440
But after breakfast, I met Mrs. Barrymore.

00:38:50.500 --> 00:38:55.131
She looked unhappy, and her eyes were red.

00:38:55.191 --> 00:38:58.332
So she did cry in the night.

00:38:58.392 --> 00:39:00.082
But why?

00:39:00.142 --> 00:39:03.543
And why did her husband lie?

00:39:03.603 --> 00:39:06.413
Was he horrible to her?

00:39:06.474 --> 00:39:09.574
I was interested in Barrymore.

00:39:09.634 --> 00:39:14.596
He had a big black beard.

00:39:14.616 --> 00:39:17.042
He found Sir Charles' body.

00:39:17.102 --> 00:39:19.510
Was he the man in the cab?

00:39:19.570 --> 00:39:23.172
Did he follow Sir Henry and Dr Mortimer in London?

00:39:23.232 --> 00:39:25.324
I needed information.

00:39:25.384 --> 00:39:30.228
My first job was to talk to the man at Grimpen Post Office.

00:39:30.288 --> 00:39:37.192
Did he give the telegram to Barrymore and only Barrymore?

00:39:37.252 --> 00:39:41.286
After breakfast, I walked to the village.

00:39:41.346 --> 00:39:43.630
It was four miles away.

00:39:43.690 --> 00:39:48.174
The man at the post office remembered the telegram very well.

00:39:48.234 --> 00:39:51.806
My boy, James delivered it, didn't you, son?

00:39:51.866 --> 00:39:54.458
Yes, father, I did.

00:39:54.518 --> 00:39:58.350
And did you give it to Mr. Barrymore himself?

00:39:58.410 --> 00:39:59.600
I asked.

00:39:59.660 --> 00:40:03.902
Well, he was upstairs, so I gave it to his wife.

00:40:03.962 --> 00:40:06.994
Did you see Mr. Barrymore?

00:40:07.054 --> 00:40:08.285
No, sir.

00:40:08.345 --> 00:40:11.458
I said he was upstairs.

00:40:11.518 --> 00:40:17.484
You didn't see him, so how do you know he was upstairs?

00:40:17.544 --> 00:40:19.314
What's the problem?

00:40:19.375 --> 00:40:20.996
Said the boy's father.

00:40:21.056 --> 00:40:23.458
Mr. Barrymore got the telegram.

00:40:23.518 --> 00:40:27.561
Why are you asking about Mr. Barrymore's telegram?

00:40:27.621 --> 00:40:31.148
Why didn't he come here to ask about it?

00:40:31.208 --> 00:40:35.556
I saw that my investigation was at an end.

00:40:35.616 --> 00:40:40.278
I walked back along the grey lonely road, and I thought.

00:40:40.338 --> 00:40:44.320
Perhaps Barrymore was our man in the cab.

00:40:44.380 --> 00:40:47.761
Was he at Baskerville Hall that day?

00:40:47.821 --> 00:40:50.322
According to his wife, he was.

00:40:50.382 --> 00:40:52.714
But was that true?

00:40:52.774 --> 00:40:56.825
Perhaps Barrymore killed Sir Charles.

00:40:56.885 --> 00:40:58.486
But why?

00:40:58.546 --> 00:41:01.675
And why did he follow Sir Henry?

00:41:01.735 --> 00:41:05.154
Why didn't he want Sir Henry at the hall?

00:41:05.214 --> 00:41:09.197
I thought about the strange message with the letters from the Times.

00:41:09.258 --> 00:41:10.648
Holmes was right.

00:41:10.708 --> 00:41:13.608
This was a very difficult case.

00:41:13.668 --> 00:41:17.360
Then, suddenly, I heard a voice behind me.

00:41:17.420 --> 00:41:21.194
I turned, and I was surprised to see a stranger.

00:41:21.254 --> 00:41:23.716
He was small and thin.

00:41:23.776 --> 00:41:25.717
He had fair hair.

00:41:25.778 --> 00:41:28.960
He was about thirty or forty years old.

00:41:29.020 --> 00:41:33.234
He had a grey suit, and he had a hat on his head.

00:41:33.294 --> 00:41:38.258
He also had a butterfly net and a box for his specimens.

00:41:38.319 --> 00:41:41.282
You must be Dr. Watson, he said.

00:41:41.342 --> 00:41:43.253
My name's Jack Stapleton.

00:41:43.313 --> 00:41:45.244
I live at Mary Pitt House.

00:41:45.304 --> 00:41:48.156
Please to meet you, I said.

00:41:48.216 --> 00:41:50.607
You're a naturalist, aren't you?

00:41:50.667 --> 00:41:53.278
But how did you know my name?

00:41:53.338 --> 00:41:56.560
I was at Dr Mortimer's house a moment ago.

00:41:56.620 --> 00:42:00.012
We saw you pass and he told me your name.

00:42:00.072 --> 00:42:03.714
I hope that Sir Henry is well after his journey.

00:42:03.774 --> 00:42:07.640
Yes, he's very well, thank you.

00:42:07.700 --> 00:42:11.064
I'm happy that he's here at Baskerville Hall.

00:42:11.124 --> 00:42:14.726
Do you know the story of the Baskerville Hound?

00:42:14.786 --> 00:42:16.468
Yes, I do.

00:42:16.528 --> 00:42:19.680
But Sir Henry doesn't believe in the supernatural.

00:42:19.740 --> 00:42:22.022
He isn't superstitious.

00:42:22.082 --> 00:42:25.884
A lot of people around here believe in the Hound.

00:42:25.944 --> 00:42:29.541
They say they can hear it at night too.

00:42:29.601 --> 00:42:34.067
He smiled, but I saw that he was worried.

00:42:34.128 --> 00:42:37.829
I'm sure that it was the reason for Sir Charles' death.

00:42:37.889 --> 00:42:41.630
He was a nervous man, and he had a bad heart.

00:42:41.690 --> 00:42:48.623
Sir Charles believed the curse, but perhaps he really did see something that night on the path.

00:42:48.684 --> 00:42:49.904
I don't know.

00:42:49.924 --> 00:42:54.886
I was very sad about his death.

00:42:54.946 --> 00:42:57.472
I liked him very much.

00:42:57.533 --> 00:43:00.710
So, did a dog chase him?

00:43:00.770 --> 00:43:02.711
Did he die of fright?

00:43:02.771 --> 00:43:06.514
I can't think of another reason, can you?

00:43:06.574 --> 00:43:10.556
At the moment, I haven't got any ideas at all.

00:43:10.616 --> 00:43:12.758
And what about Mr. Holmes?

00:43:12.818 --> 00:43:15.529
Has he got any ideas?

00:43:15.590 --> 00:43:19.292
I was surprised to hear Holmes' name.

00:43:19.352 --> 00:43:24.386
Oh, we all know about the famous Sherlock Holmes.

00:43:24.446 --> 00:43:28.234
So, of course, we all know your name too.

00:43:28.294 --> 00:43:33.853
When Dr. Mortimer told me your name, I immediately knew it was you.

00:43:33.913 --> 00:43:39.225
The fact that you're here means that Mr. Holmes is interested in the case.

00:43:39.285 --> 00:43:41.936
What does he think about it?

00:43:41.996 --> 00:43:43.547
I'm sorry.

00:43:43.607 --> 00:43:46.498
I can't answer that question at the moment.

00:43:46.558 --> 00:43:49.039
Does he plan to visit us?

00:43:49.099 --> 00:43:51.030
He can't leave London.

00:43:51.090 --> 00:43:53.411
He's working on another case.

00:43:53.471 --> 00:43:56.289
What about your investigations?

00:43:56.349 --> 00:43:58.087
Do you need any help?

00:43:58.147 --> 00:44:00.698
Please ask me anytime.

00:44:00.758 --> 00:44:04.472
I'm here as a friend to Sir Henry, that's all.

00:44:04.532 --> 00:44:06.804
I don't need any help.

00:44:06.864 --> 00:44:09.716
Excellent, said Stapleton.

00:44:09.776 --> 00:44:10.816
You're right.

00:44:10.877 --> 00:44:12.498
You must be careful.

00:44:12.558 --> 00:44:16.190
I'm sorry I asked so many questions.

00:44:16.250 --> 00:44:19.913
We reached a small path in the road.

00:44:19.973 --> 00:44:22.645
I could see a house in the distance.

00:44:22.705 --> 00:44:25.582
That's Mary Pit House, he said.

00:44:25.642 --> 00:44:28.169
Come and meet my sister."

00:44:28.229 --> 00:44:30.351
I was pleased.

00:44:30.411 --> 00:44:34.294
It was a good opportunity to study the neighbours.

00:44:34.354 --> 00:44:37.717
It's a beautiful place, the more.

00:44:37.778 --> 00:44:39.429
I know it well.

00:44:39.489 --> 00:44:44.364
We only came here two years ago, just after Sir Charles came.

00:44:44.424 --> 00:44:48.764
I love walking, so I know the more very well.

00:44:48.824 --> 00:44:55.132
The houses over there are prehistoric, Neolithic man lived in them.

00:44:55.192 --> 00:44:56.842
And look there.

00:44:56.902 --> 00:45:00.393
That's the great Grimpen Maya.

00:45:00.453 --> 00:45:04.774
It looks green and friendly, but it's a terrible place.

00:45:04.834 --> 00:45:07.724
It's dangerous when the weather is dry.

00:45:07.784 --> 00:45:12.546
Now, after the autumn rain, it's almost impossible to cross it.

00:45:12.606 --> 00:45:15.798
Every year, people die drying.

00:45:15.859 --> 00:45:19.862
Every year, 10 or 20 horses die there too.

00:45:19.922 --> 00:45:22.814
The poor animals don't understand.

00:45:22.874 --> 00:45:29.248
But I can go to the very centre of the mire and return alive.

00:45:29.308 --> 00:45:33.772
But why do you want to go to a horrible place like that?

00:45:33.832 --> 00:45:35.459
Why does anyone?

00:45:35.519 --> 00:45:39.318
because it's full of rare plants and butterflies.

00:45:39.378 --> 00:45:41.319
How interesting.

00:45:41.379 --> 00:45:43.630
I like butterflies a lot.

00:45:43.690 --> 00:45:46.262
Perhaps I can go one day.

00:45:46.322 --> 00:45:48.284
Don't be a fool.

00:45:48.344 --> 00:45:50.016
It's too dangerous.

00:45:50.076 --> 00:45:54.518
I can get there because I remember some of the rocks and plants.

00:45:54.578 --> 00:45:57.671
It's too dangerous for you.

00:45:57.731 --> 00:46:03.256
Suddenly, we heard the low howl of a dog.

00:46:03.316 --> 00:46:06.256
It was long and sad.

00:46:06.316 --> 00:46:07.946
What's that?

00:46:08.006 --> 00:46:09.516
I said.

00:46:09.576 --> 00:46:12.668
The moors are strange place.

00:46:12.728 --> 00:46:16.920
People say it's the hound of the Baskavilles.

00:46:16.980 --> 00:46:20.763
I sometimes hear that sound when I walk out here.

00:46:20.783 --> 00:46:30.650
I didn't believe the curse of the hound of the Baskavilles.

00:46:30.710 --> 00:46:38.650
But, Stapleton, what was that terrible howl on the maw?

00:46:38.710 --> 00:46:40.242
I asked again.

00:46:40.302 --> 00:46:42.654
You're an educated man.

00:46:42.714 --> 00:46:46.087
You don't believe those stories about the hound.

00:46:46.148 --> 00:46:48.280
What could the sound be?

00:46:48.340 --> 00:46:51.061
What makes a sound like that?

00:46:51.121 --> 00:46:54.132
Well, there's a very rare bird.

00:46:54.192 --> 00:46:55.694
It's called a bitten.

00:46:55.754 --> 00:46:57.946
It makes a very strange sound.

00:46:58.006 --> 00:46:59.166
That's possible.

00:46:59.226 --> 00:47:00.878
Oh, just a moment.

00:47:00.938 --> 00:47:01.928
What's that?

00:47:01.988 --> 00:47:04.461
Excuse me, Dr. Watson, I must go.

00:47:04.481 --> 00:47:08.304
That butterfly, it's a cyclopides.

00:47:08.364 --> 00:47:13.308
He ran after the butterfly towards the Grimpen Maya.

00:47:13.368 --> 00:47:19.225
Stapleton ran and jumped, and I watched him get to the island in the center.

00:47:19.285 --> 00:47:22.459
He knew the Maya very well.

00:47:22.519 --> 00:47:26.662
Just then, I heard a person behind me.

00:47:26.723 --> 00:47:29.804
I turned and saw a woman.

00:47:29.864 --> 00:47:32.557
Go back, she said.

00:47:32.617 --> 00:47:35.520
Go back to London immediately.

00:47:35.580 --> 00:47:37.241
But why?

00:47:37.301 --> 00:47:38.332
I asked.

00:47:38.392 --> 00:47:40.634
I was very surprised.

00:47:40.694 --> 00:47:42.765
I can't explain.

00:47:42.825 --> 00:47:44.947
Please go back to London.

00:47:45.007 --> 00:47:46.618
Don't come here again.

00:47:46.678 --> 00:47:49.778
Now, quiet, my brother's coming.

00:47:49.839 --> 00:47:53.500
Hello, Beryl, he said.

00:47:53.560 --> 00:47:58.162
But I didn't think he was very happy to see his sister.

00:47:58.222 --> 00:48:00.044
Hello, Jack.

00:48:00.104 --> 00:48:03.636
You're very hot, said Miss Stableton.

00:48:03.696 --> 00:48:07.779
Yes, I saw her cyclopides and I chased it.

00:48:07.840 --> 00:48:10.222
He looked at us both.

00:48:10.282 --> 00:48:12.122
I see.

00:48:12.183 --> 00:48:15.425
Now you know Dr. Watson.

00:48:15.485 --> 00:48:17.866
Are you Dr. Watson?

00:48:17.926 --> 00:48:19.634
Sherlock Holmes, his friend.

00:48:19.694 --> 00:48:23.232
But I thought you were Sir Henry Baskerville.

00:48:23.292 --> 00:48:26.844
She looked a little worried.

00:48:26.904 --> 00:48:30.695
We walked to Mary Pit House.

00:48:30.755 --> 00:48:33.426
It looked dark and sad.

00:48:33.486 --> 00:48:35.518
We went inside.

00:48:35.578 --> 00:48:37.868
I looked out of the window.

00:48:37.928 --> 00:48:41.520
The only view was of the lonely moor.

00:48:41.580 --> 00:48:44.642
Why do they live here, I thought?

00:48:44.702 --> 00:48:47.880
It's a sad, dark place.

00:48:47.940 --> 00:48:51.308
It's a strange place to live, isn't it?"

00:48:51.368 --> 00:48:52.970
said Stapleton.

00:48:53.030 --> 00:48:56.121
I had a school in the north of England.

00:48:56.181 --> 00:49:00.374
Unfortunately, one winter, some of the boys became ill.

00:49:00.434 --> 00:49:02.284
Three of them died.

00:49:02.344 --> 00:49:04.266
The school closed.

00:49:04.326 --> 00:49:09.108
I didn't have a lot of money, but I had the money to buy this place.

00:49:09.168 --> 00:49:10.749
I like it here.

00:49:10.809 --> 00:49:15.570
Dartmoor's a good place for my hobby, and my sister likes it here, too.

00:49:15.630 --> 00:49:21.362
We have our books, and we have our studies, and we have our interesting neighbours."

00:49:21.422 --> 00:49:22.712
That's right.

00:49:22.772 --> 00:49:24.264
Isn't it, Beryl?

00:49:24.324 --> 00:49:27.726
Oh, yes, she said quickly.

00:49:27.786 --> 00:49:31.218
Dr Mortimer is an interesting man.

00:49:31.278 --> 00:49:34.630
Poor Sir Charles was also a good friend.

00:49:34.690 --> 00:49:37.682
We knew him well, and we miss him.

00:49:37.742 --> 00:49:41.097
I would like to meet Sir Henry, his nephew.

00:49:41.157 --> 00:49:44.591
Come to the hall this afternoon," I said.

00:49:44.651 --> 00:49:47.232
You can meet him then.

00:49:47.292 --> 00:49:51.974
I said goodbye and walked across the moor.

00:49:52.034 --> 00:49:59.168
After about five minutes, I was very surprised to see Miss Stapleton in front of me.

00:49:59.228 --> 00:50:02.049
I must be quick, she said.

00:50:02.109 --> 00:50:03.920
Don't tell my brother.

00:50:03.980 --> 00:50:07.141
Please forget everything that I said to you.

00:50:07.201 --> 00:50:09.666
I thought you was a Henry.

00:50:09.726 --> 00:50:12.212
I can't forget it.

00:50:12.272 --> 00:50:15.765
And why must Sir Henry go back to London?

00:50:15.825 --> 00:50:18.317
The curse of the Hound.

00:50:18.378 --> 00:50:20.289
Sir Henry is in danger.

00:50:20.349 --> 00:50:22.271
Now I must go.

00:50:22.331 --> 00:50:24.954
She walked away.

00:50:25.014 --> 00:50:28.156
I went back to Baskerville Hall.

00:50:28.216 --> 00:50:30.258
I was worried.

00:50:30.319 --> 00:50:34.157
I wrote my report to Holmes.

00:50:34.217 --> 00:50:39.605
Now I plan to use my reports to Holmes and my diary.

00:50:39.665 --> 00:50:43.786
They give the reader a complete account of events.

00:50:43.846 --> 00:50:53.840
Baskerville Hall October 13th Dear Holmes, I told you about the prisoner in my last report.

00:50:53.900 --> 00:50:56.452
Now I've got more news.

00:50:56.512 --> 00:50:59.953
The prisoner escaped two weeks ago.

00:51:00.013 --> 00:51:02.564
Nobody knows where he is.

00:51:02.624 --> 00:51:05.123
Where's he finding food?

00:51:05.183 --> 00:51:07.672
Is he still on the maw?

00:51:07.732 --> 00:51:11.533
I'm worried about the Stapleton's in their lonely house.

00:51:11.593 --> 00:51:13.644
Sir Henry's worried, too.

00:51:13.704 --> 00:51:17.905
He asked Perkins the driver to sleep at their house.

00:51:17.965 --> 00:51:20.795
Mr. Stapleton said no.

00:51:20.856 --> 00:51:25.347
I think Sir Henry likes Miss Stapleton very much.

00:51:25.407 --> 00:51:27.468
She's a beautiful woman.

00:51:27.528 --> 00:51:30.839
Almost a warm, Latin beauty.

00:51:30.899 --> 00:51:34.373
It's strange that her brother is so cold.

00:51:34.433 --> 00:51:37.447
He's got a lot of power over her.

00:51:37.508 --> 00:51:39.739
She looks at him all the time.

00:51:39.799 --> 00:51:41.860
She wants to please him.

00:51:41.920 --> 00:51:44.121
I hope he's kind to her.

00:51:44.182 --> 00:51:46.874
He sometimes looks quite hard.

00:51:46.934 --> 00:51:50.936
Anyway, here are the facts.

00:51:50.996 --> 00:51:55.188
Stapleton came to the hall on that first day.

00:51:55.248 --> 00:52:01.395
The next morning, he showed us the place where the evil Sir Hugo died in 1647.

00:52:01.455 --> 00:52:05.150
It was a horrible, lonely place.

00:52:05.210 --> 00:52:07.580
So Henry didn't like it.

00:52:07.640 --> 00:52:11.271
Stapleton clearly believes this horrible curse.

00:52:11.331 --> 00:52:14.952
He believes there's a hound on the mall.

00:52:15.012 --> 00:52:18.593
We had lunch at Mary Pit House.

00:52:18.653 --> 00:52:22.474
So Henry met Miss Stapleton for the first time.

00:52:22.534 --> 00:52:24.284
They liked each other.

00:52:24.344 --> 00:52:27.346
Now they see each other every day.

00:52:27.406 --> 00:52:31.459
They have an invitation for dinner at the hall tonight.

00:52:31.519 --> 00:52:34.840
We have an invitation to go there next week.

00:52:34.900 --> 00:52:36.740
It's strange.

00:52:36.801 --> 00:52:40.871
But Mr. Stapleton doesn't seem very happy about this.

00:52:40.932 --> 00:52:45.253
He looks angry when Sir Henry talks to his sister.

00:52:45.313 --> 00:52:50.494
Perhaps he can see a lonely life in the future without her.

00:52:50.554 --> 00:52:54.414
But I think he's selfish to think that.

00:52:54.474 --> 00:53:01.578
I also met another neighbour the other day, Mr. Franklin of Laughter Hall.

00:53:01.638 --> 00:53:04.851
He's an interesting old man with a red face.

00:53:04.912 --> 00:53:08.063
He likes the stars and the night sky.

00:53:08.124 --> 00:53:11.256
There's a telescope on the roof of his house.

00:53:11.316 --> 00:53:15.169
At the moment, he's looking for the prisoner with it.

00:53:15.229 --> 00:53:19.712
Now, I must tell you about the Barrymores.

00:53:19.772 --> 00:53:22.565
I told you about the telegram.

00:53:22.626 --> 00:53:28.160
Was Barrymore the butler in London that day or was he here?

00:53:28.220 --> 00:53:30.012
We don't know.

00:53:30.072 --> 00:53:33.423
Sir Henry decided to ask him about it.

00:53:33.483 --> 00:53:35.854
He asked lots of questions.

00:53:35.915 --> 00:53:39.446
He seemed quite hard with Barrymore.

00:53:39.506 --> 00:53:44.440
Later in the evening, Barrymore spoke to Sir Henry.

00:53:44.500 --> 00:53:49.290
Barrymore doesn't understand why Sir Henry is suspicious.

00:53:49.350 --> 00:53:53.710
After this, Sir Henry felt sorry for Barrymore.

00:53:53.770 --> 00:53:58.803
The next morning he gave some of his old clothes to Barrymore.

00:53:58.863 --> 00:54:01.764
The butler was very pleased.

00:54:01.824 --> 00:54:05.867
I'm interested in Mrs. Barrymore too.

00:54:05.927 --> 00:54:08.398
She cries a lot.

00:54:08.458 --> 00:54:12.034
Is Barrymore a violent man?

00:54:12.094 --> 00:54:16.769
Then, last night, I woke up suddenly.

00:54:16.829 --> 00:54:19.360
Someone was outside my room.

00:54:19.420 --> 00:54:21.141
I looked out.

00:54:21.201 --> 00:54:24.692
There was a man at the end of the corridor.

00:54:24.752 --> 00:54:26.974
It was Barrymore.

00:54:27.034 --> 00:54:30.185
He walked very quietly.

00:54:30.245 --> 00:54:33.086
He didn't have any shoes on.

00:54:33.146 --> 00:54:35.196
I followed him.

00:54:35.256 --> 00:54:38.536
He went into one of the empty rooms.

00:54:38.596 --> 00:54:40.346
The door was open.

00:54:40.406 --> 00:54:43.728
I could see the light from his candle.

00:54:43.788 --> 00:54:45.989
I looked into the room.

00:54:46.050 --> 00:54:49.471
Barrymore was at the window with his candle.

00:54:49.532 --> 00:54:52.012
He watched for a long time.

00:54:52.072 --> 00:54:56.355
Then suddenly he turned, but he didn't see me.

00:54:56.415 --> 00:54:58.636
I ran back to my room.

00:54:58.696 --> 00:55:02.286
A few minutes later he passed my door.

00:55:02.346 --> 00:55:07.428
You only want the facts, Holmes, so there they are.

00:55:07.488 --> 00:55:16.132
Baskerville Hall October 15th Dear Holmes, here is my next report.

00:55:16.192 --> 00:55:21.316
The next morning, I went to the room at the end of the corridor.

00:55:21.376 --> 00:55:25.238
Its window has an excellent view of the moor.

00:55:25.299 --> 00:55:31.445
I'm sure that Barrymore is interested in something or someone out there.

00:55:31.505 --> 00:55:35.199
After breakfast, I told Sir Henry about it.

00:55:35.259 --> 00:55:37.200
He wasn't surprised.

00:55:37.260 --> 00:55:40.501
Sir Henry also hears Barrymore at night.

00:55:40.561 --> 00:55:43.782
We're planning to follow him tonight.

00:55:43.842 --> 00:55:48.524
After our conversation, Sir Henry decided to go out.

00:55:48.584 --> 00:55:50.595
I wanted to go with him.

00:55:50.655 --> 00:55:52.266
He wanted to go alone.

00:55:52.286 --> 00:55:55.797
He wanted to meet Miss Stapleton.

00:55:55.857 --> 00:55:58.676
This was a difficult problem.

00:55:58.736 --> 00:56:01.956
My instructions from you are clear, Holmes.

00:56:02.016 --> 00:56:04.077
I can't leave him alone.

00:56:04.137 --> 00:56:06.488
But I understood his reasons.

00:56:06.548 --> 00:56:09.780
He clearly wanted to be alone with her.

00:56:09.840 --> 00:56:14.412
I decided to follow him, but at a distance.

00:56:14.472 --> 00:56:17.964
I walked quickly towards Merippet House.

00:56:18.024 --> 00:56:23.688
At first, I couldn't see Sir Henry at all, so I climbed a hill.

00:56:23.748 --> 00:56:27.312
Then I saw him with Miss Stapleton.

00:56:27.372 --> 00:56:30.265
Sir Henry tried to kiss Miss Stapleton.

00:56:30.325 --> 00:56:32.386
She didn't want him to.

00:56:32.446 --> 00:56:35.778
Then I saw another person on the moor.

00:56:35.838 --> 00:56:39.719
It was Mr. Stapleton with his green butterfly net.

00:56:39.780 --> 00:56:42.761
He ran towards them and shouted.

00:56:42.821 --> 00:56:45.222
He seemed angry with them.

00:56:45.282 --> 00:56:49.844
Then he walked away, and his sister followed him.

00:56:49.904 --> 00:56:52.945
Sir Henry walked towards the hall.

00:56:53.005 --> 00:56:55.670
He looked very sad.

00:56:55.730 --> 00:57:01.707
I was sorry for Sir Henry, so I went down the hill to meet him.

00:57:01.767 --> 00:57:04.928
He was confused about Stapleton.

00:57:04.988 --> 00:57:11.230
Sir Henry wants to marry Miss Stapleton, and he can't understand her brother's behaviour.

00:57:11.290 --> 00:57:15.642
Stapleton says he's sorry and that he's selfish.

00:57:15.702 --> 00:57:18.393
He doesn't want his life to change.

00:57:18.453 --> 00:57:24.545
He asked Sir Henry to wait for three months before asking Miss Stapleton to marry him.

00:57:24.605 --> 00:57:29.488
Now Holmes, let me tell you about Barrymore.

00:57:29.548 --> 00:57:34.892
The first night we waited in Sir Henry's room until three o'clock.

00:57:34.952 --> 00:57:36.144
Nothing.

00:57:36.204 --> 00:57:38.766
We tried again last night.

00:57:38.826 --> 00:57:42.968
Just after two o'clock we heard someone in the corridor.

00:57:43.029 --> 00:57:44.710
It was Barrymore.

00:57:44.770 --> 00:57:47.162
He went into the empty room.

00:57:47.222 --> 00:57:48.942
We looked in.

00:57:49.002 --> 00:57:53.337
There he was, with his candle and the window again.

00:57:53.397 --> 00:57:58.199
Sir Henry walked into the room, Barrymore went pale.

00:57:58.259 --> 00:58:03.940
Sir Henry asked Barrymore to explain, but Barrymore was silent.

00:58:04.000 --> 00:58:09.362
I took the candle from Barrymore and moved it in front of the window.

00:58:09.422 --> 00:58:13.732
After a few seconds I saw a light on the moor.

00:58:13.792 --> 00:58:16.780
Someone answered my signal.

00:58:16.840 --> 00:58:23.199
Suddenly we heard a woman's voice and Mrs. Barrymore came into the room.

00:58:23.259 --> 00:58:26.180
She explained everything.

00:58:26.240 --> 00:58:32.704
The man on the moor is her brother, Selden, the escaped prisoner.

00:58:32.764 --> 00:58:36.897
She can't leave her brother alone on the moor without help.

00:58:36.957 --> 00:58:38.777
He needs food.

00:58:38.838 --> 00:58:43.968
He shows a light and Barrymore takes the food to him.

00:58:44.028 --> 00:58:48.598
Sir Henry and I decided to get Selden.

00:58:48.658 --> 00:58:54.542
I got my gun and we went out onto the moor towards the light.

00:58:54.602 --> 00:59:02.140
Suddenly we heard it again, that long low horrible howl.

00:59:02.200 --> 00:59:05.216
Sir Henry seemed a little afraid.

00:59:05.276 --> 00:59:09.210
He thought the howl came from the Grimpen mire.

00:59:09.270 --> 00:59:11.542
He was probably right.

00:59:11.602 --> 00:59:15.904
I think Sir Henry was afraid because of the curse.

00:59:15.964 --> 00:59:21.749
I think he remembered that there were a hound's footprints next to his uncle's body.

00:59:21.809 --> 00:59:25.862
We went on in the dark towards the light.

00:59:25.922 --> 00:59:30.240
Finally we arrived, but there wasn't anyone there.

00:59:30.300 --> 00:59:33.728
Then we saw Selden in the moonlight.

00:59:33.788 --> 00:59:38.352
We ran towards him, but he was fast and we couldn't catch him.

00:59:38.413 --> 00:59:40.154
He escaped.

00:59:40.214 --> 00:59:42.686
We turned to go home.

00:59:42.746 --> 00:59:46.520
Then a strange thing happened.

00:59:46.580 --> 00:59:53.462
On a hill, in front of us in the moonlight, I saw a tall stranger.

00:59:53.522 --> 00:59:56.350
The man saw us and went away.

00:59:56.410 --> 01:00:00.764
I wanted to follow him, but Sir Henry was very tired.

01:00:00.824 --> 01:00:02.766
We went home.

01:00:02.826 --> 01:00:06.008
This morning we told the soldiers.

01:00:06.068 --> 01:00:08.990
I hope they can find Selden.

01:00:09.051 --> 01:00:11.863
Finish your case quickly, Holmes.

01:00:11.923 --> 01:00:15.036
We need you here.

01:00:15.096 --> 01:00:19.764
Diary entry October the 16th.

01:00:19.824 --> 01:00:23.380
It's a wet, foggy day.

01:00:23.440 --> 01:00:26.351
Sir Henry seems very unhappy.

01:00:26.411 --> 01:00:28.292
I'm also worried.

01:00:28.352 --> 01:00:30.842
I think this place is dangerous.

01:00:30.902 --> 01:00:34.523
I don't believe the story is about the Hound.

01:00:34.583 --> 01:00:38.264
I'm not superstitious like Stapleton or Mortimer.

01:00:38.324 --> 01:00:42.224
People here say it's a horrible thing to see.

01:00:42.284 --> 01:00:47.507
I don't think the stories are true, but I know there's something out there.

01:00:47.568 --> 01:00:51.871
It howls like a hound, but where is it?

01:00:51.932 --> 01:00:56.026
Where can a gigantic dog live on the moor?

01:00:56.086 --> 01:00:58.568
Where does it find food?

01:00:58.628 --> 01:01:02.322
What about the man on the hill last night?

01:01:02.382 --> 01:01:05.962
Is he the man we saw in London?

01:01:06.022 --> 01:01:09.550
A stranger is still following us.

01:01:09.610 --> 01:01:11.601
I must find out about him.

01:01:11.661 --> 01:01:17.154
I need an answer to this problem, but I don't want to tell Sir Henry about it."

01:01:17.214 --> 01:01:21.216
This morning Barry Moore came to talk to us.

01:01:21.276 --> 01:01:24.008
He had some important information.

01:01:24.068 --> 01:01:29.350
He knew why Sir Charles went to the gate the night he died.

01:01:29.410 --> 01:01:32.752
Sir Charles had a letter from a woman.

01:01:32.812 --> 01:01:34.872
He went to meet her.

01:01:34.932 --> 01:01:39.524
Mrs. Barrymore found a piece of the letter in the fireplace.

01:01:39.584 --> 01:01:43.548
It was still possible to read the end of the letter.

01:01:43.608 --> 01:01:49.873
It was a woman's writing, and it said, Be at the gate at ten o'clock.

01:01:49.934 --> 01:01:52.456
Burn this letter.

01:01:52.516 --> 01:02:10.979
At the bottom were the letters L L Chapter 5 The Man on the Hill Diary entry October 17th It rained all day again today.

01:02:11.039 --> 01:02:13.949
I thought about the prisoner on the moor.

01:02:14.009 --> 01:02:15.790
Poor man.

01:02:15.850 --> 01:02:19.380
Then I thought about the stranger on the hill.

01:02:19.440 --> 01:02:23.441
He was on the moor in this horrible weather too.

01:02:23.501 --> 01:02:24.812
Why?

01:02:24.872 --> 01:02:26.972
Who was he?

01:02:27.032 --> 01:02:32.310
In the evening I put on my coat and went back to the hill.

01:02:32.370 --> 01:02:34.618
There was no one there.

01:02:34.678 --> 01:02:39.274
As I walked back, Dr. Mortimer drove past me.

01:02:39.334 --> 01:02:42.876
He stopped, and I got into his carriage.

01:02:42.936 --> 01:02:44.608
He's worried.

01:02:44.668 --> 01:02:47.210
His little dog is missing.

01:02:47.270 --> 01:02:50.234
He lost her on the moor yesterday.

01:02:50.294 --> 01:02:52.316
I'm sorry for him.

01:02:52.376 --> 01:02:54.383
I hope he finds her.

01:02:54.443 --> 01:02:58.464
I asked him about the letters L.L.

01:02:58.524 --> 01:03:01.878
He knows a woman in the town of Coom Tracy.

01:03:01.938 --> 01:03:04.272
She's called Laura Lyons.

01:03:04.332 --> 01:03:06.754
Perhaps she wrote the letter.

01:03:06.814 --> 01:03:09.441
She's Franklin's daughter.

01:03:09.501 --> 01:03:15.318
She married an artist called Lyons, but her father didn't like the man.

01:03:15.378 --> 01:03:17.508
Her father was right.

01:03:17.569 --> 01:03:20.110
Lyons was a horrible man.

01:03:20.170 --> 01:03:21.800
He left her.

01:03:21.860 --> 01:03:24.342
A lot of people here help her.

01:03:24.402 --> 01:03:26.954
They sometimes give her a little money.

01:03:27.014 --> 01:03:31.618
Sometimes Sir Charles gave her money too.

01:03:31.678 --> 01:03:36.912
After dinner, I talked to Barrymore about Selden.

01:03:36.972 --> 01:03:45.664
Barrymore took food for him three days ago, but he didn't see Selden's signal last night or two nights ago.

01:03:45.724 --> 01:03:48.935
He doesn't know where Selden is now.

01:03:48.995 --> 01:03:57.214
Barrymore surprised me, because he knows about the stranger on the moor too, Selden told him.

01:03:57.274 --> 01:04:03.804
The stranger lives in the prehistoric houses and a boy brings him food.

01:04:03.864 --> 01:04:07.396
Yes, I need to find out.

01:04:07.456 --> 01:04:12.908
Why is someone living on the moor in this terrible weather?

01:04:12.968 --> 01:04:18.882
The following morning I told Sir Henry about law reliance and the letter.

01:04:18.942 --> 01:04:23.204
He was very interested and very surprised.

01:04:23.264 --> 01:04:27.278
She wanted to meet him at the moor gate at ten o'clock.

01:04:27.338 --> 01:04:34.722
But that's exactly where and when my uncle died, go to Coom Tracy, talk to this woman.

01:04:34.783 --> 01:04:40.635
I arrived in Coom Tracy, and I asked about Laura Lyons.

01:04:40.695 --> 01:04:45.216
People there knew her, and it was easy to find her house.

01:04:45.277 --> 01:04:51.509
She was surprised to see a stranger, but she asked me to come inside.

01:04:51.569 --> 01:04:57.525
I'm here because I want to talk about Charles Baskerville, I said.

01:04:57.586 --> 01:05:00.320
What can I tell you about him?

01:05:00.380 --> 01:05:02.932
He was a very kind man.

01:05:02.992 --> 01:05:05.332
He helped me a lot.

01:05:05.392 --> 01:05:08.063
Did you write to him?

01:05:08.123 --> 01:05:10.854
She looked a little angry.

01:05:10.914 --> 01:05:14.375
I wrote to him once or twice to say thank you.

01:05:14.435 --> 01:05:16.505
He gave me some money.

01:05:16.566 --> 01:05:19.186
He was very kind.

01:05:19.246 --> 01:05:23.328
Did you ask Sir Charles to meet you?

01:05:23.388 --> 01:05:24.850
I asked.

01:05:24.910 --> 01:05:26.343
Really, sir.

01:05:26.403 --> 01:05:28.284
That's a very strange question.

01:05:28.344 --> 01:05:29.824
Of course I didn't.

01:05:29.884 --> 01:05:30.954
Oh.

01:05:31.014 --> 01:05:32.915
I think you did.

01:05:32.975 --> 01:05:37.246
In fact, you wrote to him on the day he died.

01:05:37.306 --> 01:05:41.108
You wanted to meet him at the more gate at ten o'clock.

01:05:41.168 --> 01:05:43.848
She went pale.

01:05:43.908 --> 01:05:45.978
Yes.

01:05:46.038 --> 01:05:47.909
Yes.

01:05:47.969 --> 01:05:50.990
I did write a letter.

01:05:51.050 --> 01:05:53.041
But he burnt it.

01:05:53.101 --> 01:05:54.752
I know he did.

01:05:54.812 --> 01:05:57.225
How do you know about it?

01:05:57.285 --> 01:05:59.588
It was a private letter.

01:05:59.648 --> 01:06:02.522
A piece of the letter didn't burn.

01:06:02.582 --> 01:06:05.785
The letters LL were on it.

01:06:05.845 --> 01:06:10.941
Why did you want to meet him at that time and at that place?

01:06:11.001 --> 01:06:13.552
He had plans.

01:06:13.612 --> 01:06:17.014
He wanted to go to London on May 5th.

01:06:17.074 --> 01:06:20.926
I needed his help before he went to London.

01:06:20.986 --> 01:06:23.587
I was busy until 10 o'clock that night.

01:06:23.647 --> 01:06:25.988
I had to meet him in the garden.

01:06:26.048 --> 01:06:29.720
A woman can't go into a single man's house at night.

01:06:29.780 --> 01:06:31.661
It's not correct.

01:06:31.722 --> 01:06:35.884
That's why I wanted to meet him by the gate.

01:06:35.944 --> 01:06:39.716
What did you do when you arrived?

01:06:39.777 --> 01:06:41.944
I didn't go.

01:06:42.004 --> 01:06:45.594
Before I went, someone came to see me.

01:06:45.654 --> 01:06:48.257
He gave me the help that I needed.

01:06:48.317 --> 01:06:53.332
But please, I can't tell you his name.

01:06:53.392 --> 01:06:57.064
Her story was probably true.

01:06:57.124 --> 01:07:00.108
But why did she go so pale?

01:07:00.168 --> 01:07:02.960
What did she want to hide?

01:07:03.020 --> 01:07:08.313
I said goodbye, and Perkins drove me towards the hall.

01:07:08.373 --> 01:07:13.164
On the way home, we saw Mr. Franklin in his garden.

01:07:13.225 --> 01:07:16.116
He invited me for a glass of wine.

01:07:16.176 --> 01:07:18.608
I sent Perkins home.

01:07:18.668 --> 01:07:21.770
Franklin was an interesting man.

01:07:21.830 --> 01:07:25.213
He talked about the more and about the stars.

01:07:25.273 --> 01:07:28.015
He showed me his telescope.

01:07:28.075 --> 01:07:32.338
I'm using this to watch the prisoner, he said.

01:07:32.398 --> 01:07:35.160
A young boy brings him food every day.

01:07:35.220 --> 01:07:38.810
Look, Watson, there he is now on that hill.

01:07:38.870 --> 01:07:41.839
I looked over towards the hill.

01:07:41.899 --> 01:07:45.110
Yes, there was a boy there.

01:07:45.170 --> 01:07:47.351
He had a parcel with him.

01:07:47.411 --> 01:07:51.363
I saw him go towards the prehistoric houses.

01:07:51.423 --> 01:07:53.964
Now I knew where the stranger was.

01:07:54.024 --> 01:07:56.535
I decided to investigate.

01:07:56.595 --> 01:07:59.876
Well, I must go now, Mr. Franklin.

01:07:59.937 --> 01:08:01.337
Thank you for the wine.

01:08:01.397 --> 01:08:04.846
I enjoyed our interesting conversation too.

01:08:04.906 --> 01:08:10.237
I walked up the hill and looked at the prehistoric houses.

01:08:10.297 --> 01:08:12.899
Only one had a roof.

01:08:12.958 --> 01:08:16.440
The man lived here, I was sure.

01:08:16.500 --> 01:08:19.091
I quietly went inside.

01:08:19.151 --> 01:08:20.732
It was empty.

01:08:20.792 --> 01:08:27.375
The parcel of food was on the floor, and there was a small place for a bed in the corner.

01:08:27.435 --> 01:08:30.967
I decided to wait for the stranger.

01:08:31.026 --> 01:08:34.386
I sat in the dark with my gun.

01:08:34.446 --> 01:08:37.376
I waited for a long time.

01:08:37.436 --> 01:08:40.790
Then I heard someone outside.

01:08:40.850 --> 01:08:44.044
I sat very quietly.

01:08:44.104 --> 01:08:48.359
Then I heard a voice.

01:08:48.418 --> 01:08:51.793
It's a beautiful evening, Watson.

01:08:51.852 --> 01:08:54.041
Why don't you come outside?

01:08:54.101 --> 01:08:57.101
Holmes, it's you!"

01:08:57.161 --> 01:08:59.164
I ran outside.

01:08:59.224 --> 01:09:01.707
I'm so happy to see you.

01:09:01.767 --> 01:09:05.635
But how did you know it was me in here?

01:09:05.695 --> 01:09:08.349
You spoke to Cigarette over there.

01:09:08.409 --> 01:09:11.850
It says Bradley of Oxford Street on it.

01:09:11.910 --> 01:09:16.783
How many men on Dartmoor by their cigarettes in Oxford Street?

01:09:16.842 --> 01:09:18.763
But how did you find me?

01:09:18.783 --> 01:09:22.535
I wasn't very careful that night on the hill.

01:09:22.595 --> 01:09:24.616
You saw me, I know.

01:09:24.676 --> 01:09:27.687
But how did you know which house I was in?

01:09:27.747 --> 01:09:29.237
It was your boy.

01:09:29.297 --> 01:09:30.528
I saw him.

01:09:30.588 --> 01:09:34.168
But why are you living like this?

01:09:34.228 --> 01:09:37.229
I'm investigating, but in secret.

01:09:37.289 --> 01:09:38.799
Cartwright's helping me.

01:09:38.859 --> 01:09:40.710
He's a very good boy.

01:09:40.770 --> 01:09:43.380
Now Watson, what do you know?

01:09:43.440 --> 01:09:44.790
Tell me.

01:09:44.851 --> 01:09:48.542
I told Holmes about Laura Lyons.

01:09:48.601 --> 01:09:51.432
That's very interesting.

01:09:51.492 --> 01:09:56.432
I think Laura Lyons is in love with Stapleton.

01:09:56.492 --> 01:10:01.123
I also know that Miss Stapleton isn't Mr. Stapleton's sister.

01:10:01.183 --> 01:10:03.254
She's his wife.

01:10:03.314 --> 01:10:08.516
So that's why Mr. Stapleton was angry with Sanri that day.

01:10:08.576 --> 01:10:10.036
But why?

01:10:10.096 --> 01:10:13.587
Why are they pretending to be brother and sister?

01:10:13.647 --> 01:10:17.338
He doesn't want people to know he's married.

01:10:17.398 --> 01:10:19.899
Stapleton's our man, Watson.

01:10:19.959 --> 01:10:22.570
Stapleton's our killer, I'm sure.

01:10:22.630 --> 01:10:25.441
But are you sure she's his wife?

01:10:25.501 --> 01:10:26.843
Yes.

01:10:26.903 --> 01:10:30.246
Do you remember your first conversation?

01:10:30.306 --> 01:10:34.318
He told you about his school in the north of England.

01:10:34.378 --> 01:10:37.169
A lot of the things he said do you are false.

01:10:37.229 --> 01:10:39.000
But these were true.

01:10:39.060 --> 01:10:44.452
Yes, he's interested in butterflies and he was once a teacher.

01:10:44.512 --> 01:10:49.204
Yes, three boys died at his school.

01:10:49.264 --> 01:10:51.975
With those facts it was easy.

01:10:52.035 --> 01:10:53.646
I found the school.

01:10:53.706 --> 01:10:57.130
After that, the rest was easy too.

01:10:57.189 --> 01:10:59.384
But he's married.

01:10:59.444 --> 01:11:02.186
What about Paul Law Reliance?

01:11:02.246 --> 01:11:03.508
Yes.

01:11:03.568 --> 01:11:05.028
Paul Woman.

01:11:05.088 --> 01:11:07.762
She wants a divorce from her husband.

01:11:07.822 --> 01:11:13.246
I think she wants to marry Stapleton and she needs his help with money.

01:11:13.306 --> 01:11:16.390
She doesn't know he's already married.

01:11:16.450 --> 01:11:18.752
We need to talk to her again.

01:11:18.812 --> 01:11:20.259
We need to tell her.

01:11:20.319 --> 01:11:23.256
Now, Watson, let's go up to the hall.

01:11:23.316 --> 01:11:26.216
Baskerville is alone there, and I don't like it.

01:11:26.276 --> 01:11:28.626
Stapleton's a killer, Watson.

01:11:28.686 --> 01:11:30.817
A killer.

01:11:30.877 --> 01:11:38.868
Suddenly, in the darkness, there was a terrible, low howl, and it came from the moor.

01:11:38.928 --> 01:11:41.939
The hound, cried Holmes.

01:11:41.999 --> 01:11:44.639
Oh no, Stapleton's out there.

01:11:44.699 --> 01:11:47.610
Then we heard a terrible scream.

01:11:47.670 --> 01:11:49.530
He's got Sir Henry!

01:11:49.590 --> 01:11:54.694
Holmes quickly ran in the direction of the scream I ran behind him.

01:11:54.754 --> 01:11:59.376
We stopped at the bottom of the hill, but we couldn't see anything.

01:11:59.436 --> 01:12:01.907
Then I saw it.

01:12:01.967 --> 01:12:03.978
It was a man's body.

01:12:04.038 --> 01:12:06.500
He was faced down on the ground.

01:12:06.560 --> 01:12:08.280
He was dead.

01:12:08.340 --> 01:12:14.064
Holmes lit a match, and in the light we saw the dead man's jacket.

01:12:14.124 --> 01:12:16.335
It was Sir Henry's jacket.

01:12:16.395 --> 01:12:19.482
The dead man was Sir Henry.

01:12:19.542 --> 01:12:21.460
Oh, no!

01:12:21.520 --> 01:12:24.463
Why did I leave Sir Henry alone today?

01:12:24.523 --> 01:12:27.046
Oh, why did I go to Coom Tracy?

01:12:27.106 --> 01:12:31.059
Why did Sir Henry go on to the more alone?

01:12:31.119 --> 01:12:34.503
Holmes went over to Sir Henry's body.

01:12:34.562 --> 01:12:36.554
He turned it over.

01:12:36.615 --> 01:12:38.946
Then he shouted.

01:12:39.006 --> 01:12:40.998
He's got a beard.

01:12:41.058 --> 01:12:42.479
This isn't Sir Henry.

01:12:42.540 --> 01:12:44.332
This is the prisoner Selden.

01:12:44.392 --> 01:12:46.922
Sir Henry is alive.

01:12:46.982 --> 01:12:51.452
Of course, Sir Henry gave some clothes to Barrymore.

01:12:51.512 --> 01:12:53.904
Barrymore probably gave them to Selden.

01:12:53.964 --> 01:12:57.186
That's why Selden's wearing Sir Henry's jacket.

01:12:57.246 --> 01:12:58.377
Hello?

01:12:58.437 --> 01:12:59.608
Who's this?

01:12:59.668 --> 01:13:00.869
Said Holmes.

01:13:00.928 --> 01:13:02.500
Someone's coming.

01:13:02.560 --> 01:13:04.390
It's probably Stapleton.

01:13:04.450 --> 01:13:06.012
Be careful.

01:13:06.072 --> 01:13:09.704
Stapleton arrived and looked at the body.

01:13:09.764 --> 01:13:11.215
Who's that?

01:13:11.275 --> 01:13:12.806
He said.

01:13:12.866 --> 01:13:17.064
It's Selden, the prisoner from Prince Town.

01:13:17.124 --> 01:13:20.600
Stapleton's face was pale.

01:13:20.660 --> 01:13:23.251
How horrible!

01:13:23.311 --> 01:13:25.001
Is he dead?

01:13:25.061 --> 01:13:28.532
Yes, he probably broke his neck.

01:13:28.592 --> 01:13:32.102
We were on the hill over there and we heard a scream.

01:13:32.162 --> 01:13:35.353
We ran down here and found him.

01:13:35.413 --> 01:13:37.633
I heard a scream too.

01:13:37.693 --> 01:13:39.254
That's why I'm here.

01:13:39.314 --> 01:13:41.704
I was worried about Sir Henry.

01:13:41.764 --> 01:13:45.465
I invited him to my house tonight, but he didn't come.

01:13:45.525 --> 01:13:48.494
Did you hear any other sounds?

01:13:48.554 --> 01:13:49.943
No.

01:13:50.003 --> 01:13:50.603
Why?

01:13:50.623 --> 01:13:56.525
Oh, you know, people talk about the hound on the maw.

01:13:56.585 --> 01:13:59.726
What do you think, Mr. Holmes?

01:13:59.786 --> 01:14:01.146
I'm right, aren't I?

01:14:01.206 --> 01:14:03.116
You are Sherlock Holmes.

01:14:03.176 --> 01:14:05.547
Well, what do you think?

01:14:05.607 --> 01:14:08.138
Yes, you're right.

01:14:08.198 --> 01:14:11.988
But no, we didn't hear anything.

01:14:12.048 --> 01:14:14.419
We found this poor man here.

01:14:14.479 --> 01:14:17.450
I think he fell and broke his neck.

01:14:17.510 --> 01:14:19.968
That's what I think.

01:14:20.028 --> 01:14:22.108
Stapleton relaxed.

01:14:22.128 --> 01:14:25.511
"'I'm happy you're here,' he said.

01:14:25.531 --> 01:14:28.994
"'Now you can help Dr. Watson with this problem.'

01:14:29.014 --> 01:14:32.617
"'I'm sorry, I can't,' said Holmes.

01:14:32.637 --> 01:14:34.979
"'I still have a case in London.

01:14:34.999 --> 01:14:37.792
"'I need to go back there.'

01:14:37.852 --> 01:14:40.233
We covered the body.

01:14:40.294 --> 01:14:47.055
Stapleton went back to Meripid House and Holmes and I went back to the hall.

01:14:47.115 --> 01:14:51.344
We are near to the end now, said Holmes.

01:14:51.403 --> 01:14:53.985
Did you see Stableton's face?

01:14:54.045 --> 01:14:57.287
He was very shocked when he saw Selden.

01:14:57.347 --> 01:15:01.820
I'm sorry, he knows I'm here, but there's nothing we can do.

01:15:01.880 --> 01:15:05.881
Now, how can we catch him, Watson?

01:15:05.942 --> 01:15:07.232
How?

01:15:07.292 --> 01:15:09.494
Let's talk to the police tonight.

01:15:09.554 --> 01:15:11.084
We know he's our man.

01:15:11.144 --> 01:15:12.696
Proof, Watson.

01:15:12.756 --> 01:15:14.236
We need proof.

01:15:14.296 --> 01:15:17.224
All we have is a body and a dog.

01:15:17.284 --> 01:15:19.872
There's no connection with Stapleton.

01:15:19.932 --> 01:15:21.942
The police need proof.

01:15:22.002 --> 01:15:25.073
But there's Sir Charles' death.

01:15:25.133 --> 01:15:28.494
Yes, but again we need proof.

01:15:28.554 --> 01:15:33.235
You and I know that he died of fright, but where's the proof?

01:15:33.295 --> 01:15:35.015
No, Watson.

01:15:35.075 --> 01:15:36.876
We must wait.

01:15:36.936 --> 01:15:40.246
Just one more thing, said Holmes.

01:15:40.306 --> 01:15:46.958
When we arrive at Baskerville Hall, don't tell Sir Henry about the Hound.

01:15:47.018 --> 01:15:54.678
Sir Henry was pleased to see Holmes, but my first job was to see Barrymore and his wife.

01:15:54.738 --> 01:15:57.539
I told them about Selden.

01:15:57.599 --> 01:16:01.580
Mrs. Barrymore cried and cried.

01:16:01.640 --> 01:16:04.440
To her, he wasn't a horrible man.

01:16:04.500 --> 01:16:06.710
He was her little brother.

01:16:06.770 --> 01:16:09.401
I was sorry for her.

01:16:09.461 --> 01:16:16.080
Then we told Sir Henry about Selden, but we didn't talk about the how.

01:16:16.140 --> 01:16:20.431
I stayed in the house all morning," said Sir Henry.

01:16:20.491 --> 01:16:22.332
It was very boring.

01:16:22.392 --> 01:16:24.583
I got a message from Stapleton.

01:16:24.643 --> 01:16:26.614
He invited me to dinner tonight.

01:16:26.674 --> 01:16:28.585
But I did as you asked.

01:16:28.645 --> 01:16:30.586
I didn't go out.

01:16:30.646 --> 01:16:34.578
Selden had your jacket, said Holmes.

01:16:34.638 --> 01:16:36.819
We thought you were dead.

01:16:36.879 --> 01:16:39.050
It was a terrible shock.

01:16:39.110 --> 01:16:42.772
I imagined Barrymore gave it to Selden.

01:16:42.832 --> 01:16:46.717
Yes, probably, said Sir Henry.

01:16:46.777 --> 01:16:51.201
Now Holmes, have you got any news for us?

01:16:51.261 --> 01:16:53.742
Things are going well.

01:16:53.802 --> 01:16:56.503
I think we're near the end.

01:16:56.562 --> 01:17:01.653
It was very late, but we went into the dining room for dinner.

01:17:01.714 --> 01:17:05.204
Holmes looked at the paintings on the wall.

01:17:05.264 --> 01:17:07.105
He smiled.

01:17:07.165 --> 01:17:09.006
Yes.

01:17:09.066 --> 01:17:12.126
Things are going very well.

01:17:12.186 --> 01:17:15.500
These pictures are very interesting.

01:17:15.560 --> 01:17:18.236
I think some of them are very good.

01:17:18.296 --> 01:17:20.088
That's a Reynolds.

01:17:20.148 --> 01:17:22.600
And this one here is a Nella.

01:17:22.660 --> 01:17:25.762
Are they all family portraits?

01:17:25.822 --> 01:17:29.324
Yes, they are, said Sir Henry.

01:17:29.384 --> 01:17:32.107
Barrymore's teaching me all their names.

01:17:32.167 --> 01:17:34.619
This is Sir William Baskerville.

01:17:34.679 --> 01:17:36.231
He was a politician.

01:17:36.290 --> 01:17:38.793
This is Admiral Baskerville.

01:17:38.852 --> 01:17:41.353
He went to the West Indies.

01:17:41.413 --> 01:17:44.252
What about this one here?

01:17:44.312 --> 01:17:47.264
That's the evil Sir Hugo.

01:17:47.324 --> 01:17:54.876
It's strange because he doesn't look evil, but the date is on the back, 1647.

01:17:54.936 --> 01:17:59.317
After dinner, Sir Henry went to his room.

01:17:59.377 --> 01:18:03.408
Holmes looked again at the picture of Sir Hugo.

01:18:03.468 --> 01:18:06.433
Do you see it Watson?

01:18:06.493 --> 01:18:10.008
I looked at the man with a large hat.

01:18:10.068 --> 01:18:14.538
He had long, curly hair and a thin face.

01:18:14.598 --> 01:18:19.149
He looks a little bit like Sir Henry, I said.

01:18:19.209 --> 01:18:22.320
Holmes got onto a chair.

01:18:22.380 --> 01:18:26.780
He put his hands over the hat and the long hair.

01:18:26.840 --> 01:18:29.981
Suddenly, I saw it.

01:18:30.041 --> 01:18:32.042
Stapleton.

01:18:32.102 --> 01:18:35.148
Stapleton is a basketball.

01:18:35.208 --> 01:18:40.525
Our first piece of proof was there on the wall.

01:18:40.585 --> 01:18:50.120
Chapter 6 Catching the Killer The next morning, Holmes told the police about Selden's body.

01:18:50.180 --> 01:18:54.394
Then, at breakfast, he told us his plan.

01:18:54.454 --> 01:18:57.608
Today is a big day for all of us.

01:18:57.668 --> 01:19:00.250
But I need your help, Sir Henry.

01:19:00.310 --> 01:19:03.071
This is very, very important.

01:19:03.131 --> 01:19:07.703
You must do what I say, but you mustn't ask any questions.

01:19:07.763 --> 01:19:09.804
Can you do that?

01:19:09.864 --> 01:19:11.785
Yes, I can.

01:19:11.845 --> 01:19:13.306
Good.

01:19:13.366 --> 01:19:17.638
You've got an invitation for dinner with the Stapleton's tonight.

01:19:17.698 --> 01:19:19.046
Is that right?

01:19:19.106 --> 01:19:21.916
Yes, and Watson's coming.

01:19:21.976 --> 01:19:23.947
Do you want to come to?

01:19:24.007 --> 01:19:25.718
No, I'm sorry.

01:19:25.778 --> 01:19:28.589
Watson and I must go to London.

01:19:28.649 --> 01:19:31.450
So Henry looked worried.

01:19:31.510 --> 01:19:35.844
But these days, I don't like being alone here.

01:19:35.904 --> 01:19:37.608
Trust me.

01:19:37.668 --> 01:19:40.499
Go to dinner with the Stapleton's.

01:19:40.559 --> 01:19:45.062
Tell them that we're very sorry, but we've got important business in London.

01:19:45.122 --> 01:19:47.703
Please give them that message.

01:19:47.763 --> 01:19:52.576
When you arrive at Mary Pit House, send Perkins home.

01:19:52.636 --> 01:19:56.578
Tell the Stapleton's that you want to walk home.

01:19:56.638 --> 01:20:00.815
Walk across the moor at night alone.

01:20:00.875 --> 01:20:03.441
Yes, but don't worry.

01:20:03.501 --> 01:20:05.322
Go straight to the hall.

01:20:05.382 --> 01:20:07.724
Stay on the path.

01:20:07.784 --> 01:20:10.726
We said goodbye to Sir Henry.

01:20:10.786 --> 01:20:15.298
Perkins took us to the station, then went home to the hall.

01:20:15.358 --> 01:20:18.540
Young Cartwright was at the station.

01:20:18.600 --> 01:20:21.452
There's a telegram for you, sir.

01:20:21.512 --> 01:20:23.684
Thank you, Cartwright.

01:20:23.744 --> 01:20:25.995
Holmes looked at the message.

01:20:26.055 --> 01:20:27.836
It said, arrive 540.

01:20:27.876 --> 01:20:29.936
Lestrade.

01:20:29.996 --> 01:20:32.395
Gird.

01:20:32.455 --> 01:20:34.516
It's from Detective Lestrade.

01:20:34.576 --> 01:20:38.217
Now, Stapleton needs proof we're in London.

01:20:38.277 --> 01:20:40.177
He mustn't think we're here.

01:20:40.237 --> 01:20:44.048
Cartwright takes the train to London when you arrive.

01:20:44.108 --> 01:20:47.499
Send this telegram to Sir Henry.

01:20:47.559 --> 01:20:51.420
I left my diary in my room.

01:20:51.480 --> 01:20:54.140
I need it urgently.

01:20:54.200 --> 01:20:59.612
Send it to me at Baker Street as soon as possible.

01:20:59.672 --> 01:21:01.305
Holmes.

01:21:01.365 --> 01:21:03.718
Do you understand?

01:21:03.778 --> 01:21:05.699
Yes, sir.

01:21:05.759 --> 01:21:08.350
Watson, come with me.

01:21:08.410 --> 01:21:11.240
I want to talk to Laura Lyons.

01:21:11.300 --> 01:21:15.211
Mrs. Lyons was surprised to see us.

01:21:15.272 --> 01:21:19.373
There are some facts missing from your story, Mrs. Lyons.

01:21:19.433 --> 01:21:22.974
We need more information, said Holmes.

01:21:23.034 --> 01:21:26.044
I told your friend everything.

01:21:26.104 --> 01:21:28.019
Not everything.

01:21:28.079 --> 01:21:34.805
You asked the Charles to meet you at the gate at ten o'clock, the time and place of his death.

01:21:34.865 --> 01:21:37.086
What's the connection?

01:21:37.146 --> 01:21:39.596
There isn't a connection.

01:21:39.656 --> 01:21:43.348
This is a case of murder, Mrs. Lyons.

01:21:43.408 --> 01:21:48.020
The case involves your friend, Mr. Stapleton, and his wife.

01:21:48.080 --> 01:21:49.610
His wife?

01:21:49.670 --> 01:21:53.642
But Mr. Stapleton's single, he lives with his sister.

01:21:53.702 --> 01:21:55.224
I'm sorry.

01:21:55.284 --> 01:21:57.218
But that's not true.

01:21:57.278 --> 01:21:59.630
She's really his wife.

01:21:59.690 --> 01:22:03.202
Here's a photograph of them from four years ago.

01:22:03.262 --> 01:22:07.164
On the back it says, Mr. and Mrs. Van de Leur.

01:22:07.224 --> 01:22:11.298
But you can see the people in the picture are the Stapertons.

01:22:11.358 --> 01:22:15.396
Poor Laura Lyons was very shocked.

01:22:15.456 --> 01:22:19.834
Mr. Holmes, this man asked me to marry him.

01:22:19.894 --> 01:22:21.674
He lied to me.

01:22:21.734 --> 01:22:24.016
He told me to write that letter.

01:22:24.076 --> 01:22:25.997
He is an evil man.

01:22:26.058 --> 01:22:28.328
Ask me anything you want."

01:22:28.388 --> 01:22:31.631
Did Stapleton dictate that letter?

01:22:31.691 --> 01:22:33.992
Yes, every word of it.

01:22:34.052 --> 01:22:38.726
With Sir Charles' money, he said a divorce from my husband was possible.

01:22:38.786 --> 01:22:41.077
Then he could marry me.

01:22:41.137 --> 01:22:43.168
I believed him.

01:22:43.228 --> 01:22:48.229
After I wrote the letter, he told me not to go to Baskerville Hall.

01:22:48.289 --> 01:22:51.140
He told me not to meet Sir Charles.

01:22:51.200 --> 01:22:53.542
He wanted to give me the money himself.

01:22:53.602 --> 01:22:57.004
He didn't want Sir Charles to give me money.

01:22:57.064 --> 01:23:02.936
Then, the next day, you read about Sir Charles' death in the newspaper.

01:23:02.996 --> 01:23:04.505
Is that right?

01:23:04.565 --> 01:23:09.416
Yes, Stapleton told me not to say anything about the letter.

01:23:09.476 --> 01:23:11.656
He said it looked bad for me.

01:23:11.716 --> 01:23:15.028
After that, I didn't trust him.

01:23:15.088 --> 01:23:17.200
You're very lucky.

01:23:17.260 --> 01:23:20.552
Stapleton's an evil man.

01:23:20.612 --> 01:23:25.164
Later, Holmes and I went back to the station.

01:23:25.224 --> 01:23:31.287
The London train arrived, and a small, strong-looking man got off the train.

01:23:31.347 --> 01:23:33.674
He walked towards us.

01:23:33.734 --> 01:23:35.410
Anything good?"

01:23:35.470 --> 01:23:36.802
he said.

01:23:36.862 --> 01:23:40.404
Very, very good, Lestrade said Holmes.

01:23:40.464 --> 01:23:43.316
Let's talk about it over dinner.

01:23:43.376 --> 01:23:50.542
Holmes told Lestrade the whole story, but he didn't talk about his plans.

01:23:50.602 --> 01:23:53.844
Finally, I asked about them.

01:23:53.903 --> 01:23:55.735
What are your plans?

01:23:55.795 --> 01:23:57.386
We need to know, Holmes.

01:23:57.446 --> 01:23:59.976
We need to know what to do.

01:24:00.036 --> 01:24:02.113
Don't worry.

01:24:02.174 --> 01:24:05.445
Trust me," he said.

01:24:05.504 --> 01:24:10.266
After dinner, we took a cab towards Meripit House.

01:24:10.326 --> 01:24:14.878
When we arrived, Holmes finally gave us some instructions.

01:24:14.938 --> 01:24:18.740
We were about 200 yards from the house.

01:24:18.800 --> 01:24:21.100
Be very quiet.

01:24:21.160 --> 01:24:23.372
Walk on Tiptoe.

01:24:23.432 --> 01:24:25.420
Let's hide here.

01:24:25.480 --> 01:24:28.500
Now, Watson, you know this house.

01:24:28.560 --> 01:24:30.730
There's a light in those windows there.

01:24:30.790 --> 01:24:32.510
What's that room?

01:24:32.570 --> 01:24:34.431
That's the kitchen.

01:24:34.491 --> 01:24:37.192
And the windows there are the dining room.

01:24:37.252 --> 01:24:38.372
Good.

01:24:38.432 --> 01:24:40.202
The curtains are open.

01:24:40.262 --> 01:24:42.352
Go quietly.

01:24:42.412 --> 01:24:44.193
Look inside.

01:24:44.253 --> 01:24:47.084
Tell us what you see.

01:24:47.144 --> 01:24:51.325
I walked down the path very quietly.

01:24:51.384 --> 01:24:54.524
I looked in through the dining room window.

01:24:54.584 --> 01:24:59.385
There were two men inside, Stapleton and Sir Henry.

01:24:59.445 --> 01:25:02.386
Stapleton's wife wasn't there.

01:25:02.446 --> 01:25:04.577
I watched them.

01:25:04.637 --> 01:25:08.619
Then Stapleton went out of the room.

01:25:08.678 --> 01:25:10.860
Henry sat down.

01:25:10.920 --> 01:25:13.340
He looked very pale.

01:25:13.400 --> 01:25:18.742
I heard a door open and the sound of shoes on the path.

01:25:18.802 --> 01:25:21.074
It was Stapleton.

01:25:21.134 --> 01:25:25.137
He went into a small building near the house.

01:25:25.196 --> 01:25:30.035
I heard some sounds inside, then he came out again.

01:25:30.095 --> 01:25:33.210
He was only in the building for a minute.

01:25:33.269 --> 01:25:36.564
I quickly went back to Holmes and Lestrade.

01:25:36.624 --> 01:25:38.694
I told them about it.

01:25:38.754 --> 01:25:41.352
But where's Stapleton's wife?

01:25:41.412 --> 01:25:42.704
Said Holmes.

01:25:42.764 --> 01:25:49.059
There are only two lights in the house, one in the kitchen, but only the servants are in there.

01:25:49.119 --> 01:25:51.390
The other is in the dining room.

01:25:51.450 --> 01:25:55.084
Only Sir Henry and Stapleton are in there.

01:25:55.144 --> 01:25:57.345
Where is she?

01:25:57.406 --> 01:26:00.248
I don't know, I said.

01:26:00.308 --> 01:26:01.800
But look!

01:26:01.860 --> 01:26:03.791
Look at the grimp and mire!

01:26:03.851 --> 01:26:07.074
The fog's coming, and it's coming towards us.

01:26:07.134 --> 01:26:09.242
It's moving very quickly.

01:26:09.302 --> 01:26:10.400
Hmm.

01:26:10.460 --> 01:26:12.340
This is bad, Watson.

01:26:12.400 --> 01:26:13.712
I don't like it.

01:26:13.772 --> 01:26:17.394
The fog is the only thing which can stop our plan.

01:26:17.454 --> 01:26:24.769
Then Holmes said, almost to himself, come away from Meribithouse, Henry.

01:26:24.829 --> 01:26:27.081
Come out soon.

01:26:27.141 --> 01:26:30.474
We waited and waited.

01:26:30.534 --> 01:26:32.906
It was now very foggy.

01:26:32.966 --> 01:26:35.578
There was no sound from the house.

01:26:35.638 --> 01:26:38.440
Then, suddenly, we heard something.

01:26:38.500 --> 01:26:39.320
Shh!

01:26:39.380 --> 01:26:40.511
Said Holmes.

01:26:40.571 --> 01:26:41.892
It's Sir Henry.

01:26:41.952 --> 01:26:43.864
Here he is at last.

01:26:43.924 --> 01:26:45.544
Shh!

01:26:45.604 --> 01:26:48.206
Sir Henry passed us.

01:26:48.266 --> 01:26:51.442
He walked quickly and he looked worried.

01:26:51.502 --> 01:26:54.799
Then, we heard another sound.

01:26:54.859 --> 01:26:57.682
It was the sound of feet.

01:26:57.742 --> 01:27:00.474
But the feet weren't those of a man.

01:27:00.534 --> 01:27:03.848
They were those of a gigantic animal.

01:27:03.908 --> 01:27:05.700
Can you hear it?

01:27:05.760 --> 01:27:08.383
There's something there, something's coming towards us.

01:27:08.443 --> 01:27:09.324
Look out!

01:27:09.384 --> 01:27:10.956
It's coming!

01:27:11.016 --> 01:27:14.916
La Strade screamed, and I took out my gun.

01:27:14.976 --> 01:27:19.574
Then, out of the fog, came a horrible animal.

01:27:19.634 --> 01:27:23.265
It was a gigantic black dog.

01:27:23.325 --> 01:27:26.316
But this wasn't an ordinary dog.

01:27:26.376 --> 01:27:30.047
It was a horrible gigantic hound.

01:27:30.107 --> 01:27:33.998
It was the hound of the Baskervilles.

01:27:34.058 --> 01:27:37.040
There was green light around its mouth.

01:27:37.100 --> 01:27:39.880
In its eyes, there was green fire.

01:27:39.940 --> 01:27:42.106
We were terrified.

01:27:42.166 --> 01:27:45.363
It's chasing Sir Henry, said Holmes.

01:27:45.423 --> 01:27:46.364
Your gun!

01:27:46.424 --> 01:27:47.566
Kill it!"

01:27:47.626 --> 01:27:49.436
I fired my gun.

01:27:49.496 --> 01:27:50.818
There was a howl.

01:27:50.878 --> 01:27:52.400
The animal was hurt.

01:27:52.460 --> 01:27:54.421
We ran towards the sound.

01:27:54.481 --> 01:27:57.364
The gigantic hound was dead.

01:27:57.424 --> 01:28:02.999
Sir Henry was on the ground, terrified and pale, but he was alive.

01:28:03.058 --> 01:28:05.070
I gave him some brandy.

01:28:05.130 --> 01:28:07.652
Thank you, Watson, he said.

01:28:07.713 --> 01:28:09.374
But what was that animal?

01:28:09.434 --> 01:28:10.564
What was it?

01:28:10.624 --> 01:28:16.478
Its eyes and its horrible mouth, they were green.

01:28:16.538 --> 01:28:19.640
I went to look at the animal.

01:28:19.700 --> 01:28:24.882
Around its eyes and its mouth, I saw something green.

01:28:24.942 --> 01:28:27.747
It was phosphorus.

01:28:27.808 --> 01:28:31.152
It's the hound of the Baskavilles.

01:28:31.212 --> 01:28:33.254
But now it's dead.

01:28:33.314 --> 01:28:34.886
You're free!"

01:28:34.946 --> 01:28:36.287
said Holmes.

01:28:36.347 --> 01:28:41.572
The green you saw was phosphorus, a phosphorus glows in the dark.

01:28:41.632 --> 01:28:45.154
Now, I'm sorry, Sir Henry, but we must hurry.

01:28:45.214 --> 01:28:49.932
We haven't got a lot of time, and we need to find our man.

01:28:49.992 --> 01:28:53.419
We went back towards Maripit House.

01:28:53.479 --> 01:28:55.019
The door was open.

01:28:55.079 --> 01:28:56.760
We ran inside.

01:28:56.820 --> 01:28:59.150
Then we heard a noise.

01:28:59.210 --> 01:29:01.931
It came from a room upstairs.

01:29:01.991 --> 01:29:05.332
We ran upstairs in the direction of the noise.

01:29:05.392 --> 01:29:07.862
Holmes opened the door of the room.

01:29:07.922 --> 01:29:10.113
There was Stapleton's wife.

01:29:10.173 --> 01:29:11.814
She was on the floor.

01:29:11.874 --> 01:29:14.574
She had a scarf round her mouth.

01:29:14.634 --> 01:29:16.195
Good God!

01:29:16.255 --> 01:29:17.025
Said Holmes.

01:29:17.085 --> 01:29:17.525
Quick!

01:29:17.585 --> 01:29:18.616
Help her!

01:29:18.676 --> 01:29:19.896
Thank you!

01:29:19.956 --> 01:29:20.934
She said.

01:29:20.994 --> 01:29:22.112
Is he safe?

01:29:22.172 --> 01:29:23.944
Is Sir Henry safe?

01:29:24.004 --> 01:29:26.976
Yes, he's safe, I said.

01:29:27.036 --> 01:29:29.858
And the hound, where is it?

01:29:29.918 --> 01:29:34.772
Don't worry, it's dead, said Holmes.

01:29:34.832 --> 01:29:36.933
Thank God.

01:29:36.993 --> 01:29:40.095
But find him, find my husband.

01:29:40.155 --> 01:29:41.786
He's a horrible man.

01:29:41.846 --> 01:29:43.738
He's cruel and evil.

01:29:43.798 --> 01:29:47.150
He keeps his hound in the middle of the Grimpen mire.

01:29:47.210 --> 01:29:48.761
That's where he is.

01:29:48.821 --> 01:29:50.480
Go and find him.

01:29:50.540 --> 01:29:53.219
But it's impossible with this fog.

01:29:53.279 --> 01:29:55.380
How can we find him?

01:29:55.440 --> 01:29:57.950
It's foggy, you say.

01:29:58.010 --> 01:29:59.791
That's good news.

01:29:59.851 --> 01:30:04.082
He ran to the center of the mire before the fog came down.

01:30:04.142 --> 01:30:08.974
He was able to get in there, but he can't get out now.

01:30:09.034 --> 01:30:13.346
He knows the way to the middle of the mire because of the rocks and plants.

01:30:13.406 --> 01:30:16.566
But in the fog, he can't get out.

01:30:16.626 --> 01:30:18.814
You've got him.

01:30:18.874 --> 01:30:23.914
And now, I'm coming to the end of my strange story.

01:30:23.974 --> 01:30:27.632
The next morning it wasn't foggy.

01:30:27.692 --> 01:30:30.004
We went to the grimp and mire.

01:30:30.064 --> 01:30:37.240
We knew it was dangerous to cross it, but Mrs. Stapleton gave us directions and we followed them carefully.

01:30:37.300 --> 01:30:40.652
The path went left and then right.

01:30:40.712 --> 01:30:42.814
It was difficult to follow.

01:30:42.874 --> 01:30:46.266
Any mistake was certain death for us.

01:30:46.326 --> 01:30:50.780
Then suddenly we saw something in the mire.

01:30:50.840 --> 01:30:52.974
It was a shoe.

01:30:53.034 --> 01:30:55.890
Holmes took a stick and got the shoe.

01:30:55.950 --> 01:30:59.394
There was a label, Myers Toronto inside.

01:30:59.454 --> 01:31:02.998
It was Sir Henry's missing shoe.

01:31:03.058 --> 01:31:07.412
Stapleton used this shoe, said Holmes.

01:31:07.472 --> 01:31:10.796
His dog needed a scent to follow Sir Henry.

01:31:10.856 --> 01:31:14.614
This shoe gave the animal the scent.

01:31:14.674 --> 01:31:18.350
We arrived at the center of the mire.

01:31:18.410 --> 01:31:23.002
Stapleton wasn't there, but this was where the hound lived.

01:31:23.062 --> 01:31:28.154
There was some food, and the dead body of a black and white dog.

01:31:28.214 --> 01:31:32.788
Look, a dead dog, said Holmes.

01:31:32.848 --> 01:31:35.558
Dr. Mortimer's dog.

01:31:35.618 --> 01:31:39.351
Poor animal, and poor Mortimer.

01:31:39.411 --> 01:31:41.362
He loved his dog.

01:31:41.421 --> 01:31:43.323
Do you know Watson?

01:31:43.383 --> 01:31:45.566
I think Stapleton's dead.

01:31:45.626 --> 01:31:47.978
I think he died in the mire.

01:31:48.038 --> 01:31:49.920
This shoes are proof.

01:31:49.979 --> 01:31:54.052
And this place is where Stapleton's hound lived.

01:31:54.112 --> 01:31:57.964
We all heard the sound of the hound on the moor.

01:31:58.024 --> 01:32:03.468
Stapleton could hide the hound, but he couldn't keep it quiet.

01:32:03.528 --> 01:32:06.018
I agreed with Holmes.

01:32:06.078 --> 01:32:09.420
Stapleton was probably dead.

01:32:09.480 --> 01:32:14.522
Back in Baker Street, London, it was the end of November.

01:32:14.582 --> 01:32:17.244
It was a cold, foggy night.

01:32:17.304 --> 01:32:20.666
Holmes and I were in the sitting room by the fire.

01:32:20.726 --> 01:32:25.498
It was good to see Sir Henry and Dr. Mortimer again, wasn't it, Holmes?

01:32:25.558 --> 01:32:27.879
I'm pleased they came this afternoon.

01:32:27.939 --> 01:32:29.170
Yes.

01:32:29.230 --> 01:32:31.551
I didn't know they were in London.

01:32:31.611 --> 01:32:33.972
It was good of them to come.

01:32:34.032 --> 01:32:36.474
It was a very interesting case.

01:32:36.534 --> 01:32:39.269
The case of their hound of the Baskervilles.

01:32:39.329 --> 01:32:46.156
Yes, but there are one or two things that I still don't understand.

01:32:46.216 --> 01:32:50.688
Let's go back to the beginning, said Holmes.

01:32:50.748 --> 01:32:54.863
First of all, the picture in the dining room.

01:32:54.923 --> 01:32:57.968
It showed us that Stapleton was a Baskerville.

01:32:58.028 --> 01:33:02.812
He was the son of Roger Baskerville, Sir Charles' third brother.

01:33:02.872 --> 01:33:05.394
Roger died in South America.

01:33:05.454 --> 01:33:09.387
We all thought Roger wasn't married, but that wasn't true.

01:33:09.447 --> 01:33:11.859
He got married and had a son.

01:33:11.919 --> 01:33:17.114
His son's name was also Roger, our man Stapleton.

01:33:17.174 --> 01:33:20.196
Years later, young Roger got married.

01:33:20.256 --> 01:33:25.513
He married Beryl Garcia, a beautiful woman from Costa Rica.

01:33:25.573 --> 01:33:29.969
Roger was a bad man, like his father.

01:33:30.029 --> 01:33:32.100
He stole a lot of money.

01:33:32.160 --> 01:33:37.084
The police wanted to talk to him, so he changed his name to Vandellur.

01:33:37.144 --> 01:33:41.406
Mr. and Mrs. Vandellur escaped to England.

01:33:41.466 --> 01:33:45.088
Here, they started their school in the north.

01:33:45.148 --> 01:33:52.473
Then, when the three school boys died, the Vandellurs changed their name again to Stapleton.

01:33:52.533 --> 01:33:54.564
They went to Dartmoor.

01:33:54.624 --> 01:33:57.835
Stapleton knew he was a Baskerville.

01:33:57.895 --> 01:34:00.826
He knew Sir Charles was rich.

01:34:00.886 --> 01:34:03.298
He decided to kill Sir Charles.

01:34:03.358 --> 01:34:08.570
Barrel pretended to be Stapleton's sister and they bought a house near Baskerville Hall.

01:34:08.630 --> 01:34:13.558
Here, Stapleton became friends with Sir Charles Baskerville.

01:34:13.617 --> 01:34:17.334
Sir Charles told him about the Hound of the Bascavilles.

01:34:17.394 --> 01:34:24.978
Stapleton knew that Sir Charles was afraid of the Hound, and he knew that Sir Charles had a weak heart.

01:34:25.038 --> 01:34:27.950
This gave Stapleton the idea.

01:34:28.010 --> 01:34:31.741
He went to London and bought a gigantic dog.

01:34:31.801 --> 01:34:34.402
It was strong and savage.

01:34:34.463 --> 01:34:37.984
He took it to Dartmore in secret.

01:34:38.044 --> 01:34:41.916
As we know, it lived at the Grimp and Meyer.

01:34:41.976 --> 01:34:45.238
This is why people sometimes heard the Hound.

01:34:45.298 --> 01:34:48.690
The idea of the Phosphorus was very clever.

01:34:48.750 --> 01:34:50.412
The dog looked evil.

01:34:50.472 --> 01:34:53.123
It looked supernatural.

01:34:53.183 --> 01:34:58.266
Sometimes, Stapleton took the dog onto the moor at night.

01:34:58.326 --> 01:35:04.112
People saw it and began to talk about the curse of the Hound of the Bascavilles.

01:35:04.172 --> 01:35:11.018
Stapleton really wanted Sir Charles to see the hound, but Sir Charles never went on to the moor at night.

01:35:11.078 --> 01:35:12.259
He was afraid.

01:35:12.319 --> 01:35:16.881
So, Stapleton asked Beryl to help him, but she refused.

01:35:16.941 --> 01:35:20.643
That's when Laura Lyons comes into the story.

01:35:20.703 --> 01:35:23.454
Stapleton became friends with her.

01:35:23.514 --> 01:35:26.026
She thought he was a single man.

01:35:26.086 --> 01:35:30.818
She wanted to divorce her horrible husband and marry Stapleton.

01:35:30.878 --> 01:35:35.440
Then, Stapleton heard about Sir Charles' trip to London.

01:35:35.500 --> 01:35:37.351
He worked very fast.

01:35:37.411 --> 01:35:40.012
He told Laura to write to Sir Charles.

01:35:40.072 --> 01:35:42.764
He told her to ask for a meeting.

01:35:42.824 --> 01:35:49.916
He gave the letter to Sir Charles, then he made up a story and told Laura not to go.

01:35:49.976 --> 01:35:54.500
That night, Stapleton went to the Grimpen Meyer.

01:35:54.560 --> 01:35:58.432
He painted the hound's eyes and mouth with the phosphorus.

01:35:58.492 --> 01:36:01.723
Then he took the dog to the morgue gate.

01:36:01.783 --> 01:36:05.595
Here it jumped over the gate and chased the Charles.

01:36:05.655 --> 01:36:08.346
So Charles died of fright.

01:36:08.406 --> 01:36:10.758
The dog didn't run on the path.

01:36:10.818 --> 01:36:12.738
It ran next to the path.

01:36:12.798 --> 01:36:15.960
That's why there were no footprints until the end.

01:36:16.020 --> 01:36:21.241
Then Stapleton called the dog and he took it back to the mire.

01:36:21.301 --> 01:36:23.810
He was very clever.

01:36:23.870 --> 01:36:25.161
There was no proof.

01:36:25.221 --> 01:36:31.012
His wife and Laura Lyons thought something was wrong, but they didn't have any proof.

01:36:31.072 --> 01:36:36.874
At first, Stapleton probably didn't know anything about Sir Henry.

01:36:36.934 --> 01:36:41.135
But after Sir Charles' death, Dr Mortimer told him.

01:36:41.196 --> 01:36:44.376
He told him about the Canadian air.

01:36:44.436 --> 01:36:49.342
Dr Mortimer came to London and Stapleton followed with his wife.

01:36:49.402 --> 01:36:51.406
He couldn't leave her on Dartmoor.

01:36:51.466 --> 01:36:52.778
He didn't trust her.

01:36:52.838 --> 01:36:55.630
He locked her in the hotel room.

01:36:55.690 --> 01:36:58.702
He followed Dr. Mortimer every day.

01:36:58.762 --> 01:37:01.444
He wore a big black beard.

01:37:01.504 --> 01:37:03.074
It was a false beard.

01:37:03.134 --> 01:37:07.088
That day, he followed Dr. Mortimer here to Baker Street.

01:37:07.148 --> 01:37:09.610
Then he followed him to the station.

01:37:09.670 --> 01:37:13.060
He saw Sir Henry and the doctor go to the hotel.

01:37:13.120 --> 01:37:17.011
Stapleton probably wanted to kill Sir Henry here in London.

01:37:17.071 --> 01:37:20.804
When he saw us, he changed his plans.

01:37:20.864 --> 01:37:24.096
His wife knew about his plans.

01:37:24.156 --> 01:37:28.678
She wanted to tell Sir Henry, but she was afraid of her husband.

01:37:28.738 --> 01:37:33.932
She cut words from the front page of the Times newspaper to make a letter.

01:37:33.992 --> 01:37:36.774
A servant gave it to Sir Henry.

01:37:36.834 --> 01:37:41.206
Stapleton needed something with Sir Henry's scent on it.

01:37:41.266 --> 01:37:43.440
He needed it for the dog.

01:37:43.500 --> 01:37:48.325
He paid a servant in the hotel, and the servant stole the shoe.

01:37:48.384 --> 01:37:52.538
But it was a new shoe, so Henry's scent wasn't on it.

01:37:52.598 --> 01:37:55.550
That's why the second shoe was missing.

01:37:55.610 --> 01:38:00.692
When Stapleton heard we were on the case, he went back to Dartmoor.

01:38:00.752 --> 01:38:03.554
That's where our story started.

01:38:03.613 --> 01:38:07.196
There's one thing I still don't understand, Holmes.

01:38:07.256 --> 01:38:09.207
Everyone knew Stapleton.

01:38:09.267 --> 01:38:10.828
Everyone knew his name.

01:38:10.888 --> 01:38:14.144
He couldn't suddenly become a Baskerville.

01:38:14.204 --> 01:38:18.148
Mrs. Stapleton told me he had many plans.

01:38:18.208 --> 01:38:21.008
One was to go back to South America.

01:38:21.068 --> 01:38:23.759
He didn't need to be in England to get the money.

01:38:23.819 --> 01:38:25.840
There were other plans, too.

01:38:25.900 --> 01:38:30.621
But you can be sure Watson Stapleton knew how to get his money.

01:38:30.681 --> 01:38:33.222
He was an evil man.

01:38:33.282 --> 01:38:37.142
Now, Watson, let's talk about something different.

01:38:37.202 --> 01:38:39.393
I've got tickets for a show.

01:38:39.453 --> 01:38:43.662
Let's have dinner at Marcini's, then go to the theatre.

01:38:43.722 --> 01:38:45.508
Can you be ready in half an hour?

